const SOP_INDEX = [{"id":"Manual_Part_1","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 1 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"GETTING STARTED\ncenter SIGNING-ON TO THE AGENT CONSOLE\n From the “Idle” state,\n Press the [SN ON] key (on Numeric keypad) \nor \nif using the mouse, click the [\nOPERATOR INFORMATION\nUpon validation, the Operator Information pop-up window will be presented. This window displays the agent\u0027s call stats since sign-on.\nAn Agent may view his/her statistics at any time during the current sign-on session by pressing the “Microsoft Application” key located next to the right-hand side [CTRL] key on the keyboard.\n� Press [Apps] + O (the letter O).\n� If using the mouse, left-click on the [Stats] Agent Shortcut Button in the lower- right corner of the screen.\n� After viewing statistics, click the [Close] button in the window or press the\n[SELECT] key on the keyboard.\nSIGNING OFF and Assigning Work FROM THE CONSOLE \n� Press the [SN OFF] key, or if using the mouse, click the [On/Off] agent shortcut button. A validation prompt will appear:\nSign-Off? Press “Y” to Validate\nSign-Off? Press “Y” to Validate\n� Type ‘Y’ to complete the ‘Sign-off’ sequence. The console will display an Idle state.\n � If pending work exists, assign the work to the dispatcher. select the dispatcher’s station # in the drop-list presented.\nThen select ‘Transfer.’ All pending pages, transmit memos, reminders will be transferred to the selected agent/console.\nThe Agent Spectrum Screen \n- \nAnswer Phrase \nDate and Time\nAccount Name\nMessage Status\nCurrent State\nSystem Call\nStatus\nCall Activity\n(Talk 1, 2, 3, 4)\nPending Work\nOperator ID\nCall Timer\nSystem \nDate and Time\nAgent \nShortcut\nButtons\nCaller ID and\nDialed Number\nPrism/SDM/Logger\nStatus indicator\nSPECIAL LOCATE\nAccount Information Screens \nand \nThe Expanded Locate Instructions Displayed\nONCALL SCHEDULER\nMESSAGE TICKET\nScreen\nACTIVE ALERTS\n00\nAnswer Phrase"},{"id":"Manual_Part_2","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 2 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Date and Time\nAccount Name\nMessage Status\nCurrent State\nSystem Call\nStatus\nCall Activity\n(Talk 1, 2, 3, 4)\nPending Work\nOperator ID\nCall Timer\nSystem \nDate and Time\nAgent \nShortcut\nButtons\nCaller ID and\nDialed Number\nPrism/SDM/Logger\nStatus indicator\nSPECIAL LOCATE\nAccount Information Screens \nand \nThe Expanded Locate Instructions Displayed\nONCALL SCHEDULER\nMESSAGE TICKET\nScreen\nACTIVE ALERTS\nThe Spectrum Agent Keyboard\nSystem\nStatus/Clear\nMessage Entry \u0026\nDelivery/Copy/Save\nCall Activity [Talk 1-4]\nDispatching/Locates/\nFile\nCall Recording\nSTATUS\nCLEAR\nENTER DELIVER UNDLVR\nIF IF\nMSG\nMSG\nREDLVR\nCOPY\nSAVE\nTALK TALK TALK \nPATCH PAGE\nDELETE CT. REM\n1\n2\n3\n4\nLOCATE\nEDIT\nREWIND\nFILE\nSTART STOP\nRECORD\nEscape\nKey\nEsc\n! 1\n@\n2\n#\n3\n$\n4\n%\n5\n\u0026\n7\n(\n9\nIMPT\nQ\nWCB EMG RC\n^\n6\nOT WBA\n*\n8\n)\n0\n_\n+\n=\nBackspace\n\nANSWER\nInsert Home\nW\nE\nR\nT\nY\nUK# PR/C O/C P/C U I O P\n{\n[\n}\n]\nDelete End\nPage\nUp\nPage Down\nDIAL REMIND FLAG\nTab\n\nCaps Lock\nPRS\n7\nTUV\n8\n*\nWXY\n9\nSN ON\nSN OFF\nASAP SVC O/D R/T GFD HC C/A RES CBR\nA S D F G H J K L\n:\n;\n“\n\u0027\nEnter\n\nGHI JKL MNO\n4 5 6\nD I S P L A\nY\nShift\nf\nHOLD\nO/P WCI\nZ X\nCANC OFC BK@ UNO APPT C V B N M\n\u003c\n,\n\u003e\n.\n?\n/\nShift\nf\nABC DEF\n2 3\nn\nAlt\nAlt\nn\nCtrl\n\n\n\n1\n\n0\nOPERATOR\n#\nS E L E C T\nHold\nKey\nAlt\nKey\nAlt\nKey\nApps\nKey\nCtrl\nKey\nNumeric Dial Pad\nSign On/Off\nSpectrum™ \nby Telescan\nSystem\nStatus/Clear\nMessage Entry \u0026\nDelivery/Copy/Save\nCall Activity [Talk 1-4]\nDispatching/Locates/\nFile\nCall Recording\nSTATUS\nCLEAR\nENTER DELIVER UNDLVR\nIF IF\nMSG\nMSG\nREDLVR\nCOPY\nSAVE\nTALK TALK TALK \nPATCH PAGE\nDELETE CT. REM\n1\n2\n3\n4\nLOCATE\nEDIT\nREWIND\nFILE\nSTART STOP\nRECORD\nEscape\nKey\nEsc\n! 1\n@\n2\n#\n3\n$\n4\n%\n5\n\u0026\n7\n(\n9\nIMPT\nQ\nWCB EMG RC\n^\n6\nOT WBA\n*\n8\n)\n0\n_\n+\n=\nBackspace\n\nANSWER\nInsert Home\nW\nE\nR\nT\nY\nUK# PR/C O/C P/C U I O P\n{\n[\n}\n]\nDelete End\nPage\nUp\nPage Down\nDIAL REMIND FLAG\nTab\n"},{"id":"Manual_Part_3","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 3 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Caps Lock\nPRS\n7\nTUV\n8\n*\nWXY\n9\nSN ON\nSN OFF\nASAP SVC O/D R/T GFD HC C/A RES CBR\nA S D F G H J K L\n:\n;\n“\n\u0027\nEnter\n\nGHI JKL MNO\n4 5 6\nD I S P L A\nY\nShift\nf\nHOLD\nO/P WCI\nZ X\nCANC OFC BK@ UNO APPT C V B N M\n\u003c\n,\n\u003e\n.\n?\n/\nShift\nf\nABC DEF\n2 3\nn\nAlt\nAlt\nn\nCtrl\n\n\n\n1\n\n0\nOPERATOR\n#\nS E L E C T\nHold\nKey\nAlt\nKey\nAlt\nKey\nApps\nKey\nCtrl\nKey\nNumeric Dial Pad\nSign On/Off\nSpectrum™ \nby Telescan\nFunction and Dual-Function Keys: Many of the function keys have dual functions. The function on the lower half of the keys can be initiated by pressing the key. Functions listed on the top-half of the keys can be initiated by pressing [SHIFT] and the key. Agent Shortcut Buttons are the colored buttons displayed on the right-hand side of the Agent console, they work similarly to the functional keystrokes and keystroke combinations as mentioned below.\nSTATUS/CLEAR\nDisconnects the agent from the line\nIf/Enter Msg\n[ENTER MSG] to generate a message ticket.\n[Shift]+ [IF/ENTER MSG to create an UF (temporary, internal) message for an account.\nIF/DELIVER MSG\n[DELIVER MSG] to display the Undelivered Message List. [DELIVER MSG] will also display the list of purple flashing Transmit Error Memos (from a blank screen and in “Standby” state). [CTRL] + [DELIVER MSG] to search the system for undelivered messages. [SHIFT]+[UNDLVR/RDLVR] to return a msg that has already been delivered back to the Undelivered Message List.\nUNDLVR/REDLVR\n[REDLVR] to display the Delivered Msg List, a list of messages that have previously been delivered in some way. [SHIFT]+[UNDLVR/RDLVR] to return a message that has already been delivered back to the Undelivered Message List.\nCOPY/SAVE"},{"id":"Manual_Part_4","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 4 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"[SAVE] to edit an undelivered message or to force a msg on to the Incomplete Message stack. [ALT]+[COPY] to make a copy of a message for a designated account AND make any necessary editing corrections, and press [FILE] to initiate.\nTALK 1-4\n[TALK] keys correspond to 1 of 4 activity windows on-screen and will be used to answer incoming calls, to dial-out and to patch\nPATCH\n[PATCH] indicates a conference call connecting an incoming call with an out-going call.\nDELETE/LOCATE EDIT\n[LOCATE EDIT] to enter or update the Locate Instructions.\n[DISPLAY]+ [LOCATE EDIT] (or use the [*] key in the Numeric keypad) to view Expanded Locate Instructions (ELI) information while answering an incoming call or when dialing out.\nCt. REM/FILE\n[FILE] to signify the completion of data entry in a message ticket. [FILE] is also used to signify the completion of any other work, like entering Locate Instructions, “IF” messages and memos.\nINSERTING/OVERWRITING TEXT\nBy default, text is entered in the “OVR” (OVERWRITE) MODE in Spectrum. This means when the cursor is placed at the beginning of an existing word or sentence, the new text that is typed will overwrite the existing test.\nDisplaying accounts and Locate instructions \nDISPLAYING AN ACCOUNT OR SUB-ACCOUNT\nDisplay a Master Account, From the Standby state,\n� Press the [DISPLAY] key (on Numeric keypad).\n� Enter a 4-Digit account number to display a master account.\n*Note: Pressing the down arrow will move to next sequential master or sub-account, the right arrow will move to the next sequential master, bypassing any sub- accounts.\nDisplay a Sub-Account while viewing a Master Account\n� Press [DISPLAY] key\n� Enter the 1 or 2-digit sub-account number, press [SELECT] to move to the sub-account."},{"id":"Manual_Part_5","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 5 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"If you are in a sub-account and you wish to go directly back to the Main screen:\nPress [Display] + [Select] - to get to main screen when in Sub-Account\nPress [Display] + [Home] - to get to main Master Account Screen\nSub-Accounts might be used for:\nto sort out different medical offices or specialists under the same medical group name.\ninternal dispatching - auto-copied messages - offices request a 2nd copy of the message to be sent to a different number, fax, email. \nTo search for an account\n Press [ALT]+S or “LEFT” click on ACCOUNTS in menu.\n Then type in the search bar the account name or a key word.\n TALK\n3100\nRING\n03\nHOLD\n02\nHOLD\n7500\nTALK\n1\nTALK\n2\nTALK\n3\nTALK\n4\n00TALK\n3100\nRING\n03\nHOLD\n02\nHOLD\n7500\nTALK\n1\nTALK\n2\nTALK\n3\nTALK\n4\nINCOMING CALLS \nANSWERING A CALL\nPress [TALK 1-4] -this selects the call and brings up the account screen. The caller is not live.\nPress [ANSWER] -This brings the caller live on the line.\nPressing [CLEAR] disconnects the call once the call is completed.\nPLACING A CALL ON UNIVERSAL HOLD\nAs an Agent, you are expected to place incoming calls on HOLD by using:\nUNIVERSAL HOLD: Placing a call on UNIVERSAL HOLD will make that call available to be picked up by all agents. The TALK key will then change to a RED HOLD.\nTo place the current caller on hold to answer another incoming call press the HOLD key. This will place the current caller on hold.\nTo place a call on HOLD you will have to modify the account’s answer phrase: \n“Benjamin Franklin, this is ___ May I Place You on Hold?”\nIf the caller says YES, say “Thank you” and put them on UNIVERSAL HOLD. If the caller says NO, don’t put them on HOLD, take the call. *If it’s an account you are not trained to manage, then let the caller know you will TRANSFER caller to someone who can assist them."},{"id":"Manual_Part_6","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 6 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"If you are not on a call and there is a spurt of calls ringing in, ANSWER all the ringing calls to put them on HOLD using the MODIFIED HOLD ANSWER PHRASE. Keep putting the calls on HOLD until the spurt stops.\nPLACING A CALL ON PRIORITY HOLD \n PHLD\n0000\nPHLD\n2222\nXFER\n1111\nXFER\n3333\nTALK\n1\nTALK\n2\nTALK\n3\nTALK\n4\n00PHLD\n0000\nPHLD\n2222\nXFER\n1111\nXFER\n3333\nTALK\n1\nTALK\n2\nTALK\n3\nTALK\n4\nPlacing a call on PRIORITY HOLD will make that call available only to the agent that initiated the Hold. (A Console can have up to four Priority Holds or Transferred Calls at once.) DO NOT place the current caller on PRIORITY HOLD no more than two times during the same call.\nTo place the current caller on hold exclusive to your console (call will not be available to other agents), you may: Press [Shift]+[HOLD] or press ALT + HOLD.CALL PHRASES\nThe following phrases are mandatory. AT ALL TIMES, every employee at Answer Arizona is to be professional, polite, and courteous to every caller. “Please” and “Thank You\" must be said with every question and statement. DO NOT SAY “UH HUH,” “WHAT,” “UMM.” We are a “MESSAGE CENTER” NOT Answering service.\nOpening phrase\n“May I ask who is calling, please?”\nWhen putting calls on hold\n“Can you hold, please.”\nReturning to a call on hold\n“Thank you for waiting. May I help you?”\nEnding phrase\n“I will ask to call regarding at (phone number). Is that correct? Thank you.”\nPatch Release\n“One moment please while I connect you to __ (clients name) _.” If the caller says thank you be sure to end the call by saying “you’re welcome”\nAnnounce Patch\n* In most cases “One moment please while I connect you to _ (client’s name).” And announce the caller and any other information required to the client."},{"id":"Manual_Part_7","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 7 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Verifying the spelling of names – SPELLING SHOULD BE VERIFIED ON ALL CALLS!!! “Will you spell your name, please?”\nRequesting a telephone number\n“Your telephone number, please?” or “May I have your telephone number, please?”\nCaller refusing to leave a telephone number.\n“May I have your telephone number for my records, please?”\n“Mr./Ms. may not have your number with him/her.”\n“Your telephone number is paged directly to Mr./Ms. .” (Make sure client has a pager.\nRequesting a message – Always repeat the phone number.\n“May I ask what this call is regarding, please?,” “What is the nature of your call, please?”\nGiving out information on the client’s return or when the message will be received. \n“I will page Mr./Ms shortly and ask him/her to return your call.” (Make sure client has a pager)\n“Mr./Ms will be checking in shortly.”\nTRANSFERRING A CALL\nTo transfer a caller to another agent console:\nPress [ALT] + T or If using the mouse, select the ‘Transfer’ agent shortcut button. \nThen type the desired station number.\nIf it\u0027s a single digit station number, then add a “0” plus the 1-digit number of the station.\nEx: Console 2 would be entered as “02”. Console 22 would be entered as “22”.\nTo Access a Transferred Call:\n PHLD\n0000\nPHLD\n2222\nXFER\n1111\nXFER\n3333\nTALK\n1\nTALK\n2\nTALK\n3\nTALK\n4\n00PHLD\n0000\nPHLD\n2222\nXFER\n1111\nXFER\n3333\nTALK\n1\nTALK\n2\nTALK\n3\nTALK\n4\nPress the [TALK 1-4] key ONCE to the corresponding “XFER” (Transfer) Activity Window \nor, if using the mouse, click on the “XFER” activity window\nThis selects the call and opens the account screens. The caller is not live at this time. \nNext Press the [ANSWER] key\nOr press the [TALK 1-4] key A SECOND TIME to bring the caller on live.\nACCOUNT ALERTS"},{"id":"Manual_Part_8","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 8 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"An Account Alert may pop up at the Agent console when an inbound call is presented to the console, if configured. The Alert must be dismissed by the operator (by pressing the spacebar) before any further action can be taken. Alerts are designed to notify agents of special conditions related to the handling of calls for the programmed account.\n To Act on an Account Alert:\n� Press [Spacebar] to close the Alert window to proceed to call processing.\nACTIVE ALERTS\nActive alerts are located in the upper left-hand corner of the Spectrum screen. This area may have important information to act upon while on the phone with the caller. Always make sure to take a glance at the active alert window when on the phone with a caller.\nIt is good to go through the accounts and familiarize yourself with any active alerts there may be.\nSpectrum On-Call Scheduler:\nThe Spectrum on-call scheduler is located to the left of the message ticket screen. The Spectrum On-Call Scheduler is an automated system that tracks our client’s schedules so that messages can be relayed accurately, day and night. \nAs an agent you will not be required to edit the on-call scheduler. You will have to refer to the information from time to time. It’s always good to take a look to see if there are any patching instructions.\nIt can also be used for on-call instructions or to show a list of doctors who are off such as in account 8601 and many other accounts.\nThe Russ Lyon Accounts are set up so that you can patch to the on-call personnel, if need be, by double clicking on the agent\u0027s name in the on-call scheduler. *This will be covered further in under the patching section.\nleft61109SPECIAL LOCATE\nAccount Information Screens \nand \nThe Expanded Locate Instructions Displayed\nONCALL SCHEDULER\nMESSAGE TICKET\nScreen"},{"id":"Manual_Part_9","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 9 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"ACTIVE ALERTS\n00SPECIAL LOCATE\nAccount Information Screens \nand \nThe Expanded Locate Instructions Displayed\nONCALL SCHEDULER\nMESSAGE TICKET\nScreen\nACTIVE ALERTS\nThe Message ticket screen is where you will record the caller\u0027s information and file it so that the dispatcher can review it and relay the message. \nMessages can be transmitted via:\nText message, E-mail, Fax\nAlpha pager\nSecure messaging\nDial-out\nAs an agent you don\u0027t really pass the message unless the message ticket is set up to be auto transmitted. The dispatcher relays the message.\nWHEN CALLERS REQUEST A SPANISH SPEAKER;\nStep 1 Press Display Key, enter account 0000.\nStep 2 Select Current Date to view dispatcher/operators on duty.\nStep 3 Search for “S” next to the dispatcher or operator’s name. “S” indicates that dispatcher or operator is a Spanish speaker.\nStep 4 Take Spanish caller off hold, TRANSFER Spanish caller to the dispatcher/operator’s station number. \nIf There are No Spanish Speakers on Duty:\nStep 1 Place the SPANISH CALLER on PRIORITY HOLD \nStep 2 Go to account 4444 and Select SPANISH SPEAKER\nStep 3 Search for SPANISH SPEAKER ON CALL in the SPECIAL LOCATE\nStep 4 Double click on the SPANISH SPEAKER ON CALL’s \u003cphone number\u003e\nStep 5 Announce you have a Spanish speaker on Account XXXX.\nStep 6 If NO ANSWER, try the B/U ON CALL.\nStep 6 If B/U NO ANSWER, connect caller to the SPANISH TRANSLATOR.\nHEARING/ SPEAKING IMPAIRED CALLERS\nHearing impaired or deaf callers may utilize a RELAY SERVICE to assist them. A CA (Communications Assistant) will assist the caller. The CA will alert the operator. (These types of calls may take longer than usual.)\nHow to assist the caller:\nYou may have to SPEAK MORE SLOWLY. The CA may be using AMERICAN SIGN LANGUAGE or may be typing in your responses or use other forms of RELAY."},{"id":"Manual_Part_10","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 10 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Speak directly to the other person. The CA is on the line to relay the call but NOT involved in the conversation. Speak as if the CA is not there and address the other party.\nTo let the caller, know that it is her/his turn to speak, say “GO AHEAD.”\nWhen call is complete, end the call with your customary “Thank you.” \nDISPLAYING THE LIST OF CALLS MANAGED: CALL HISTORY\n The system has the ability to save the last 500 calls managed by a particular agent during a session. A call list can be accessed displaying the accounts and the time the calls were answered.\n From the “Standby” state:\n� Press the [ALT]+D or If using the mouse, select the ‘History’ agent shortcut button. to display the Recent Call History. \n� Press an arrow key to move to desired account, then press [SELECT] or click on desired account using the mouse.\n� Just like most of the lists in the Spectrum Agent, the oldest call appears first; the newest call appears last in the list.\nCOLOR CODES OF CALL MANAGED:\nNote each entry lists the time, account number and name and may be color- coded.\n� Blue entries represent answered calls.\n� Amber entries represent accounts that were displayed once the call was answered.\n� Red entries indicate calls that were accessed from the holding queue.\n� Magenta entries indicate a dial-out.\n� Grey entries indicate an account that was [DISPLAY]’ed from the Agent Console.\nSELECTING A CALL IN THE CALL HISTORY AND HOW TO LISTEN TO A CALL IN THE VOICE LOGGER\nAgents can listen to previous calls in CALL HISTORY. Dispatchers may ask you to verify the caller’s information such as phone numbers, spelling of names, if call is an emergency or non-emergency, etc. \nSelect HISTORY from the Spectrum Short Cut Bar."},{"id":"Manual_Part_11","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 11 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Scroll down to locate the account name or the account number and the time you took the call.\nUsing your mouse, RIGHT CLICK over the call.\nThis will bring up the VOICE LOGGER on the BOTTOM right side of the SPECTRUM SCREEN\n[insert screen shot of voice logger box]\nThe VOICE LOGGER can also be accessed by “bypassing” the “FOR:” in the IF DEL messages by going to the ticket and right clicking on the message you need directly from the list of messages.\nHOW TO EDIT A TICKET USING THE VOICE LOGGER:\nAccess the ticket in IF DEL or UNDEL/REDELIV to edit the information if needed.\nUsing your mouse, click on the “right arrow” on the VOICE LOGGER to activate recording.\nIf corrections are needed, edit the ticket and FILE the MODIFIED ticket.\nMake sure you send a MEMO to the dispatcher confirming the edit was corrected or if the existing information is correct. \nACCOUNT INFORMATION SCREENS\n00SPECIAL LOCATE\nAccount Information Screens \nand \nThe Expanded Locate Instructions Displayed\nONCALL SCHEDULER\nACTIVE ALERTS\n00SPECIAL LOCATE\nAccount Information Screens \nand \nThe Expanded Locate Instructions Displayed\nONCALL SCHEDULER\nACTIVE ALERTS\nAs an agent looking at the information screens you are looking for instruction on: \nDo I take a Message or How do I refer to the Caller? \nWhich ticket do I use (if multiple tickets)?\nWhat information do I need to collect?\nDo I have to Patch or Announce Patch this call prior to disconnecting with the caller?\nIs there anything else I may have to address with the caller on the line?"},{"id":"Manual_Part_12","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 12 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"What is the difference between an Emergency and What is a Routine Matter? An EMERGENCY is something that cannot wait until the office returns to their normal business hours. Medical emergencies would include things like: Hospitals calling to speak to the doctor, medication reactions, emergency prescriptions (if the account accepts after-hour prescriptions) or canceling a surgery the night before. If you are uncertain about passing the caller’s message as an emergency, you can ask the caller if they feel it’s an emergency. If you’re still in doubt, ask the DISPATCHER.\nPROPERTY EMERGENCIES would include, but not limited to, broken plumbing, no electricity, or no air conditioning, etc.\nOther types of emergencies: There are many different types of industries we answer for. However, a caller’s situation might be considered an emergency in one account and may not be considered an emergency in another account. Become familiar with types of emergencies that are particular to the account.\nAn example would be a janitorial service company may consider a same day appointment cancellation an emergency and may want you to patch the caller over to the Client’s number. Yet, other accounts may not consider a same day appointment cancellation an emergency.\nROUTINE MATTER is something that can wait until the office returns to normal business hours: Paperwork, insurance matters, billing questions, customers wanting to schedule non-emergency work or schedule an appointment.\nDo I Take a Message or Where do I refer the Caller? \nThe following explanations are in general, because there are some accounts that may have exceptions to these guidelines. It is very important to look through all the accounts and familiarize yourself with those exceptions."},{"id":"Manual_Part_13","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 13 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"RETURN REFER OFFICE (RTN REF OFC): Only if it’s an EMERGENCY. Cannot wait until the office returns to their normal business hours. Non-emergency calls OPERATOR will refer caller to call office during normal business. OPERATOR will not take a message. If the caller insists on leaving a message, you can let the caller know you are available for emergencies only.\nHOW TO REFER A CALLER DURING NORMAL BUSINESS HOURS: There are several reasons why the caller may have reached the answering service during the office normal business hours. Some reasons include calls being forwarded for a meeting, computer/phone issues or lunch.\n*Always check the SPECIAL LOCATE to see if there is a reason the phones are forwarded to the answering service. \nAnother major reason is the caller may have called the incorrect office number. Verify which number the caller dialed.\n*This happens a lot when people select redial from a voicemail that they get from the office. You will just need to advise the caller of the office number or offer to patch them to the office.\nSome of the accounts are set up in this manner with the green (left) and red (right) screen. \nBe aware that these screens vary in hours and instruction from account to account. Familiarize yourself with the differences in call instruction from account to account. Familiarize yourself with the differences in call instruction from to account to account. (These screens are designed this way because Answer Arizona receives a lot of callers call the after-hours number instead of calling the office number.)"},{"id":"Manual_Part_14","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 14 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"RELAY: The OPERATOR will take the caller’s information and reason for the call on a MESSAGE TICKET. The operator will put the appropriate RELAY in the “FOR” FIELD on the ticket. The RELAY information will tell the DISPATCHER if the call is to be for the ON CALL or for the office during business hours. The RELAY information is located in the bottom left corner of the ACCOUNT INFORMATION BOX in green (see above)\nTYPES OF RELAYS ARE:\nREFER ROUTINE OFFICE (RTN REF OFC): Messages can be taken after hours only if it’s an EMERGENCY and cannot wait until the office returns to their normal business hours. Non-emergency calls OPERATOR will refer caller to call office during normal business hours, OPERATOR will not take a message. If caller insists on leaving a message, you can let the caller know you are available for emergencies only.\nHOLD ROUTINE (HLD RTN) This means OPERATORS can take a message during normal business hours and after hours (when office is closed). In the ‘FOR FIELD” the OPERATOR will enter ‘HLD RTN.” These calls are non-emergency calls.\nPASS ALL/TAKE ALL Means “take all messages,” the caller should receive a call back the same night regardless of an emergency or a routine matter. Some accounts will still want to know if it is an amergency. You may have to document that in the message ticket as a *SIDE DOCUMENT. Example: *ER See “Side Documentation in Section V.” “In the “FOR FIELD” the OPERATOR will enter OFFICE for non-emergency or ON CALL for emergency.\nPATCH/PATCH ALL – You don’t have to open a message ticket. Simply PATCH the caller to the CLEINT or Extension they desire. In the “FOR” field the OPERATOR will enter O/C *PATCHED."},{"id":"Manual_Part_15","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 15 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"ANNOUNCE PATCH – Open a message ticket and collect the requested information from the caller, then ANNOUNCE PATCH the caller over to the correct person. File the message ticket. In the “FOR” field the OPERATOR will enter O/C *Patched. (If the instructions say, “Patch to Dr O/C, which means ANNOUNCE PATCH.”\nEXPANDED LOCATE INFORMATION (ELI)\n- Account Information Screens \nand \nThe Expanded Locate Displayed\n00Account Information Screens \nand \nThe Expanded Locate Displayed\n- ACTIVE ALERTS\n00ACTIVE ALERTS\n- ONCALL SCHEDULER\n00ONCALL SCHEDULER\n- LOCATE\n00LOCATE\n\\\\\nThe dispatcher uses expanded Locate Information to obtain on-call information or instructions for accounts with multiple personnel that are o/c for different situations.\nThere are some occasions an agent will need to use the Expanded Locate to obtain certain information or instructions in order to know how to proceed with the call.\nThe Expanded Locate Instructions are set up differently for every account that has them. You will have to familiarize yourself with the different accounts. Not all instructions can be set up the same, because every office has its own way of determining who is on call.\nAs an agent you will not be required to edit the Expanded Locate Instructions (ELI). If a client calls in requesting a change to the Expanded Locate Instructions. Then you will transfer the client over to the dispatcher.\nAs an agent from time to time you will need to view the Expanded Locate Instructions. \nThe Expanded Locate Instructions (ELI) shares the same screen as the Account Information Screen\nWhen you display the Expanded Locate Instructions (ELI) you will have to toggle back and forth between the Expanded Locate Instructions and the Account Information Screens.\n To Display the Expanded Locate Instructions"},{"id":"Manual_Part_16","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 16 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Press [DISPLAY] then [EDIT LOCATE], to display ELI area.\nor press the Asterisk key [*] on the numbers pad. Using the [*] key will allow you to toggle between the expanded locate area and the first information screen.\n - The SPECIAL LOCATE\nThe Special Locate area holds up to 108 characters of short-term information for an account.\nEvery Time you take a call:\n SPECIAL LOCATE\n00SPECIAL LOCATE\nYou must LOOK At The LOCATE. \nCheck to see if there are any special instructions you may need to address with the caller while they are on the line.\n At the beginning of your shift, you should always click through ALL the LOCATES on the LOC/IF button on the right-hand side of the Spectrum window. This will keep you up to date with any immediate temporary account changes that you may have to act upon.\nHere are some examples and explanations of Special LOCATES\n - \nThis LOCATEt explains that the office stepped out to lunch from 12pm to 2pm. \nIf the caller has an emergency (ERS) then we take a msg. \nIf the caller has a routine (RTN) matter, then we advise the caller to call back at 2pm when the office returns.\n - \nThis locate explains that the office is closed for moving on 5/19 and 5/20\nIf a caller has an emergency (ERS), then we take a message. The dispatcher will notify the DR O/C. If the caller has a routine (RTN) matter, then we advise the caller to call back on Monday 5/23 when the office returns.\n- \nThis explains calls are forwarded(C/F) after 1pm on Thursdays. \nIf the caller has an emergency, then we are to Announce Patch to the office back line (BKL) TL 5pm. If a hospital calls in, then we take a message, and the dispatcher notifies the Doctor."},{"id":"Manual_Part_17","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 17 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"This explains that we are to Announce Patch all calls to Chris the O/C and the dispatcher will text the message. You will need to scroll down to find Chris’ phone number. This LOCATE information will expire 5/20 at 5pm.\nThis explains what sequence we are to Announce Patch to if it is an emergency or a routine matter. FYI, INA means If No Answer.\nThe first line of this locate is to remind the operator to check sub account 02 for messages. This would be done when the office checks in.\nOn the second line the dispatcher has already set up the o/c format for you the operator. When you see this format, you must ask the client who is on call. Also get the client\u0027s name that called in.\nYou would replace the x\u0027s with the name of the person on call and then also the name of the person that gave you the information. \nThe LOCATE is set up for when the office checks in with us. It reminds us where to check for possible extra messages and to ask the client who is on call. \nPlease be aware of how important it is to read and understand the Special locate information with the caller on the line as you may have to Announce Patch a call or advise the caller of a temporary situation.\nNot following the SPECIAL LOCATE instructions may result in delaying an emergency call out.\nBe sure to get yourself into the habit of always looking at the SPECIAL LOCATE when first answering a call.\nTO DELETE/LOCATE EDIT\nAnswer a call or display an account then,\nPress the [DELETE/LOCATE EDIT] key. Enter the new/current locate informatio\nPress the [FILE] key then the border will now appear purple.\nA SPECIAL LOCATE FOR ON CALL CHANGES MUST LOOK LIKE THIS:"},{"id":"Manual_Part_18","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 18 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Medical: (Always verify doctor is listed with contact information on screen if a doctor is not listed then we do not have contact information – ask a dispatcher FIRST before disconnecting with the client!)\nDR (name) O/C TL (date) * If DR is taking all newborns: NBS: DR (name) TL (date)\nIf DR taking other DR’s newborns: DR (name)’s NBS TO DR (name) TL (date)\nIf DR from another account on call: DR (name) O/C TL (date) * DISPLAY ACCT (number)***\nIf we are to refer another doctor’s office number: DR (name) O/C TL (date)\n***REFER (office number) ***\nIf a triage nurse is checking in, transfer to dispatcher immediately! IF the current dispatcher is backed up and there is another dispatcher available then transfer it to the backup dispatcher.\nOther: (Always verify client is listed on screen with contact information)\n(name) O/C TL (date)\nO/C: (name) TL (date)\nB/U: (name) TL (date)\n**IF YOU HAVE ANY PROBLEMS ASK THE DISPATCHER BEFORE DISCONNECTING THE CLIENT**\nNever give out PHONE NUMBERS unless it clearly states “REFER” OR “MGO” (may give out)\nUSING HYPERTEXT COMMANDS\nHypertext are indicated with a blue dot With an Information Screen displayed on-screen, to highlight a bulleted Hypertext prompt:\n00\n� Press [Shift]+[SELECT] to activate the Hypertext prompt or click once on the screen.\n� Use the arrow keys to move to the desired prompt \n� Press [SELECT] again and the command(s) will be executed.\n� \nCLICK ONCE the screen to activate the Hypertext Prompt on screen. \nPOINT AND CLICK on the desired command, this will select and execute that Hypertext command.\nYou will be unable to highlight any Hypertext prompt that cannot be executed from the current console “State.”\nThe Hypertext Prompts will perform one or more operations, such as:\nGo to or view a particular information screen."},{"id":"Manual_Part_19","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 19 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Go to or view a particular account or sub-account.\nSpeed-dial a phone or pager number.\nSelect a particular free-form message template.\nInsert Keystrokes into a message or page ticket.\nSelect a particular scripting message template. \nTYPES OF MESSAGES\nMessage Tickets with NO Labeling\nOpen a message ticket.\nPress [IF/ENTER MSG]\nLook for the call instructions \non the Information screens\n*Use [Page Up] or \n[Page Down]to go to the next page on the \ninformation screens\nTake down the caller\u0027s information on\nthe message ticket.\nBe sure to follow the order in the instructions.\nHere are some other examples of how message tickets may look.\nthese are just a few examples:\nIt is very important to always make sure to indicate if the message is to be passed as an emergency or held for when the office opens. \nIn the ER field - mark Y or N\nAlways type in the For: field either Ofc or O/C\nThis helps the dispatcher know if they need to hold the message or pass it to the on call.\nThese next two examples show that there are two pages to the message ticket.\nPress [TAB] to get to the next page.\n This next example reminds you to ask the caller if their phone accepts blocked calls. if the answer is \"NO\" Then advise the caller to unblock their phone by pressing *87 after hanging up in order to get a call back.\n*Not asking the caller about accepting blocked calls may delay an emergency response from the doctor. \nAUTO FILLED MESSAGE TICKETS\nleft \nSome Accounts request that we document every call.\nPress [IF/ENTER MSG] \nor \nThe window may automatically pop up when you [ANSWER] the account.\nNext, select the appropriate reason then. \n[FILE] the ticket\nAnnounce Patch Tickets\nWhen managing an Announce Patch call always open a message ticket and get the requested information prior to Announce Patching"},{"id":"Manual_Part_20","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 20 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Directions for patching can either be in the Special Locate, ON CALL SCHEDULAR, Expanded Locate or sometimes on the information screens. \nThis example shows the Special locate with the Announce Patch instructions.\nNotice the side note in message ticket:\nINA VMS: \"Ans AZ will text msg\"\nThis means: If NO ANSWER, operator will leave.\na voicemail stating, \"Answer Arizona will text you the message.\"\n*Patching will be covered in a later section\nPatch Tickets: You don’t have to open a MESSAGE TICKET for PATCH calls. Simply PATCH the caller over to the Client.\n*HOW TO PATCH WILL BE COVERED IN SECTION VI – MESSAGE DELIVERY\nWRITING EFFECTIVE/ACCURATE MESSAGE TICKETS\nOPERATORS MUST WRITE CLEAR AND ACCURATE messages. An OPERATOR is like a news reporter who reports accurate information and follows the concept of “who, what, when and where.”\nMessages that are incorrect or unclear can cause serious delay in getting assistance for the caller or a caller’s family member. If the air conditioner stops cooling during a heat wave and the tenant is a senior and the phone number wasn’t confirmed or the address, could cause emergency health issues. CONFIRMATION OF NUMBERS, ADDRESSES AND NAMES IS MANDATORY\nAccurate grammar\nCorrect spelling\nEasy to read and understand by the dispatcher, the on call or a nurse, etc.\nAppropriate descriptive words (buttocks, breast, urinating, nasal discharge, rectum, etc.)\nInclude all relevant details (who, what, when and where)\nWrite the message using the 1st PERSON words as if the caller is the one writing the message.\n1st PERSON PRONOUNS: I, WE, ME, MINE, MY, OUR. Example: “I need a prescription,” “My prescription wasn’t called in to the pharmacy” or “I have a question about my water heater.”\nSIDE DOCUMENTATION"},{"id":"Manual_Part_21","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 21 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"From time to time, you may have to add a side note in a message ticket to help better explain an exception or a reason to pass the call. Here are some examples of side documentation you may have to use on a message ticket:\n*C/B MISSED CALL (CALL BACK MISSED CALL)\n*N/A (NO ANSWER)\n*BKL NO ANSWR (BACKLINE NO ANSWER)\n*VM FULL (UNABLE TO LEAVE A VOICE MAIL, VOICE MAIL FULL)\nADV NO AFTR HR RX (ADVISE NO AFTER HOUR RX)\n*CLR INSISTS ER (CALLER INSISTS EMERGENCY)\n*2ND, 3RD CL (2ND OR 3RD CALL)\n*CANCEL MESSAGE\n*PATCHED\nINSERTING AND OVERWRITING TEXT\nBy default, text is entered in the \"OVR\" (Overwrite) mode in Spectrum.\nThis means that when the cursor is placed at the beginning of an existing word or sentence, the new text that is typed will overwrite the existing text.\nAn agent can press the [INSERT] key to switch to the Insert “INS” mode. \nThis will make the new text to be inserted and will not overwrite the existing text but will shift it to the right. \nTo return to the “OVR” mode, simply press the [INSERT] key again.\nThe “OVR” prompt re-appears.\n INCOMPLETES\nIncomplete messages can occur if an agent, while entering a message, answers an incoming call before [FILING] the current message.\nACTING ON THE “INCOMPLETE” MESSAGE PROMPT\nDo not allow more than 3 Incompletes. If you happen to get 3 Incompletes stop answering calls finish out the incompletes and [FILE] them.\nWhen “Incomplete” messages are present a prompt will flash in black in the pending area denoting the total number of incomplete messages residing at that console. \nAn Incomplete message can also be created by pressing the [SAVE] key while in the “Entering Msg” state before the [FILE] key is pressed. This “forces” your work to your Incomplete stack, so that you can return to “Standby” state for the next task."},{"id":"Manual_Part_22","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 22 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"WHEN THE “Incomplete” MESSAGEs, from “Standby,”\nPress the [Esc] key twice, complete any work on the Incomplete ticket.\nPress the [FILE] key to complete the message, press [Esc] twice to display the next Incomplete message.\nRepeat until all Incomplete tickets are [FILE]\u0027d.\n-Or- use your mouse to double-click on the black flashing INCOMPLETE \nTO FLIP THROUGH THE INCOMPLETE MESSAGE STACK:\nPress [Esc] twice to display the first Incomplete message.\nPress [SAVE] to place current message on bottom of incomplete stack.\nPress [Esc] twice to display the next incomplete message.\nPress the [SAVE] key again to place message on bottom of stack.\nRepeat the above steps until the desired Incomplete ticket is displayed.\nUSING THE COPY/SAVE KEY TO EDIT MESSAGES (SECTION BEING UPDATED)\nYou may only EDIT your own ticket if you made an error after filing the ticket. But, you cannot EDIT your own (original) ticket if you get another call from same person/patient wanting to change the information on the ticket.\nOPERATOR must [COPY] message to input the new information on a new ticket. (note: 3400 msg instructing to do a new ticket?)\nExamples of information change could be: \nNew phone number\nDifferent room number \nPerson missed the call from the ON CALL \nHospital calls back to change a ROUTINE CONSULT to URGENT CONSULT F\nor 2nd, 3rd or 4th calls \nCaller wants to cancel the ticket.\n*ANSWER ARIZONA MUST HAVE DOCUMENTATION OF EVERY CALL\\RECORDING*\n[SAVE] to edit an undelivered message or to force a msg on to the Incomplete Message stack.\n [ALT]+[COPY] to make a copy of a message for a designated account AND make any necessary editing corrections, and press [FILE] to initiate."},{"id":"Manual_Part_23","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 23 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"The [SAVE] key can be used to add/edit information on a Message ticket, re-direct a message to another person (change the “For” field), or to force a ticket on to the Incomplete Message stack. Modified messages are placed on the Saved Messages List (if enabled in the AMR).\nFrom the “Delivering Msg” state:\nPress [SELECT] key to display the desired message.\nPress the [SAVE] key to re-open the message ticket, the cursor will appear in the “For Field.”\nMake the necessary changes to the message ticket.\nPress [FILE] when editing is complete. The message will be marked with an ‘S’ in the status column, indicating that the message has been modified.\n *Reminder on Incomplete Messages\n Do not go over more than three incompletes. Stop answering and go back and finish out the Incomplete message tickets.\nAlso, All STAT, Stemi calls or any call where the Nurse or Doctor is saying pass it ASAP. \n- Stop answering calls and finish the message ticket then alert the dispatcher right away. \nDO NOT LET THESE TYPES OF CALLS TO THE INCOMPLETE STACK.\nDOCUMENTATION FOR 2ND AND 3RD CALLS OR CANCELING A MESSAGE:\nSECTION BEING UPDATED 8/28\nWhen a caller tells you this is their “2ND OR 3RD CALL or they want to CANCEL a previous message: Create a new message ticket, noting a SIDE DOCUMENTATION *2ND OR *3RD call or CANCEL at the end of the message. \nIf a second call, ALWAYS confirm the caller’s phone number. An OPERATOR could have entered an incorrect phone number and/or didn’t verify the number with the caller.\nYou can COPY the previous ticket by [ALT] and [COPY] keys (COPYING MESSAGES) will appear at bottom of left of screen, type in account number, pull up a new ticket, type in [FOR FIELD] *2nd call or cancel and in the body of the ticket and [FILE]"},{"id":"Manual_Part_24","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 24 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"This is very important. Our client did not receive the first call either because it failed to transmit to their text, email or the client hasn’t had an opportunity to call the caller back. This lets the dispatcher know they have to confirm a SECOND CALL\nDELIVERING MESSAGES\n Display the Client\u0027s account.\n Look to see if there are any pending messages in the \"UNDELIVERED\" stack.\n If there are undelivered messages, advise the client they have messages.\nDepending on how many messages there are the Client may either want you to verbally relay the messages to them or they may request that you fax the messages over to them. \nIf the client requests for the messages to be faxed, then alert the dispatcher and they will fax the messages.\nIf the office says they will take down the information, then verbally relay the messages:\n Press [IF/DELIVER MSG] - Entering DTF\nTYPE the Client\u0027s name in the Deliver to Field\nPress [SELECT] - records the name of client.\nPress [SELECT] again to open the first message\nverbally give the client the message starting with the date and time of the call.\nPress [FILE] - Completes the message and sends to the delivered message stack (see above 10 delivered) \nmove on to the next message by arrowing down.\nThen press [SELECT] to select the next message.\nkeep repeating until all the messages are delivered.\n *If for some reason you need to escape out of a message then press [ESC] twice, then you will be able to [ARROW UP/DOWN] to next message.\n- \n00\nOnce all the messages have been Delivered:\nUpper left corner will say No Undelivered\nBottom Center will say All Delivered\n00\nOnce all the messages have been Delivered:\nUpper left corner will say No Undelivered\nBottom Center will say All Delivered\nOFFICES CHECK OUT:"},{"id":"Manual_Part_25","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 25 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Many of the offices will call in and let us know that they are forwarding the phones. They may either be forwarding for a meeting, lunchtime or leaving for the day/weekend. They may even be calling in to let us know they are having phone/computer issues at the office. Remember most offices can be identified by the caller ID.\nBe sure to always look at the caller ID prior to placing the call on hold.\nWhen checking out or forwarding their phones the client may advise you as such:\n\"Stepping out for lunch.\" OTL\n\"Going into a meeting.\" C/F IN MTG TL 2PM\n\"We are forwarding the phones.\" TFN\n\"We are rolling the phones.\" \n\"You have our phones.\"\n\"Leaving for the day/weekend.\" GFWKND\nIf they are gone for the day or gone for the weekend GFD\nThen update the Special Locate with GFD or GFWKND\nAlso, when the office checks out, they may: \ngive a time frame of when they will return.\nadvise you of who is o/c.\ngive you instructions on how to manage emergency calls and routine matters. \nwhen the office calls in to give on-call info always get:\nthe name of the person/technician/DR on call\nthe start/end date and time of when the person/DR will be on-call.\nthe name of the Client that gave you the on-call information.\nWhenever the office gives you on-call instructions you must let the dispatcher know what they advised. Also, document what their on-call instructions are in the Special Locate. If the Client is giving you in depth or confusing on-call instructions then alert the dispatcher, they will advise you to transfer the client to them. Let the client know you will transfer them to the dispatcher who can better assist them. Do not say HOLD.\n“IF” MESSAGES\nAn “IF” Message allows a client to leave a message for a specific caller when he/she calls the service."},{"id":"Manual_Part_26","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 26 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Click on IF Message and a pop up window will display further instructions.\nWhen answering a call always take a quick look to see if there are any IF Messages. \nYou may have to address something with the caller while they are on the line.\n00Click on IF Message and a pop up window will display further instructions.\nWhen answering a call always take a quick look to see if there are any IF Messages. \nYou may have to address something with the caller while they are on the line.\nIn the example above Dr. Dishner called in to the answering service and requested that when Dr. Clark Wysong calls in and specifically asks for Dr. Dishner, then we are to patch Dr. Clark Wysong to Dr. Dishner\u0027s mobile number.\nThe IF message should always be titled with the name of the person/situation that the message is for\nHere are other examples:\nAlso, you may see IF messages used in this manner on some accounts:\n OR\nThese IF messages are to be read across. See the --\u003e\u003e\u003e this means the message carries over to the next field. This is used to relay small info quickly to the operator.\nTo Create An \"IF\" Message\n DISPLAY the account.\n Press [Shift]+ [IF ENTER]\n Fill in the fields on the IF Message ticket. \n*Always put the name of the person or situation the message is for in the FOR Field.\n Press [FILE]\nTo escape from an unwanted IF Message:\n press [Esc] twice and “C” to cancel when prompted. \n Press “C” to Cancel Message\n00Press “C” to Cancel Message\nTHREE WAYS TO PATCH A CALL: PATCH, ANNOUNCE PATCH AND DUAL PATCH:\nPatching is connecting the Caller (inbound line) to the Client (outbound line). A completed MESSAGE TICKET is not required for patching calls.\nHow to PATCH:\nSay “One moment please while I connect you to __Client’s name__.”\nPress \n[PATCH] \nPress \n[TALK 1-4]"},{"id":"Manual_Part_27","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 27 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Click on either hypertext link or you may have to dial the number yourself:\n -254000If Hypertext link:\nClick on hypertext link -\nshows speed dialing.\nClick on link second time -shows dialing out.\nOnce you hear the call ringing then,\nPress [PATCH] -brings the caller on the line.\nPress [STATUS/CLEAR] -disconnects call.\n*NOTE FOR MEDICAL ACCOUNTS\nIf the instructions are Patch to Dr. O/C, then that means Announce Patch. \nAlways Announce Patch if it says to Patch to the Dr. O/C and if no answer Leave Word to Call Answering Service (LWTCAS) as a side documentation.\nIf Dialing the Phone Number:\nPress [PATCH] \nPress [TALK 1-4]\nPress [DIAL]\n Once you hear ring tone then,\nKey-in the phone number\nPress [DIAL], a second time\n Once you hear the call ringing then,\nPress [PATCH] – Brings the caller on the line.\nPress [STATUS/CLEAR] – Disconnects the call.\n*Special note Russ Lyons Accts are setup so you can connect to their o/c floor agent by clicking on their name in the o/c scheduler.\nANNOUNCE PATCH: When you take an Announce Patch Call always open a message ticket and get the callers information that is requested from the account. Then you will Announce Patch the caller over to the requested Client’s phone number. YOU HAVE to “Announce the Call” to the Client answering, by letting them know who you have on the line. If the Client says “Okay” then release the caller to them. Sometimes the Client may want you to take a message.\nHow to ANNOUNCE PATCH:\nSay “One moment please while I connect you to __Client’s name__.”\nPress [PATCH] \nPress [TALK 1-4] \nClick or select either hypertext link/Dial phone# etc. -Dial Out \nLet the call ring until the Client you are calling answers then say: \n\"__Greeting__, this is __your name__ with the answering service,\""},{"id":"Manual_Part_28","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 28 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"\"I have __caller\u0027s name__ calling for you.\" \nyou can let the Client know what the call is regarding.\nIf the Client says go ahead and connect them over, \nPress [PATCH] -brings the caller online.\nPress [STATUS/CLEAR] -disconnects the call.\nReview message\nDocument in the message ticket *Patched in the \"For\" field and in the call notes.\nSometimes the Client you are calling may not answer and the call and it will go to voice mail. Depending on the accounts instructions you may have to do the following:\nDisconnect as soon as you hear the voicemail. \n(don\u0027t let the caller go to the Client\u0027s voice mail)\nPressing [STATUS/CLEAR] \n-disconnects the outbound call and brings the caller back on the line.\nAdvise the caller, that the Client they are trying to reach is not available and offer to take a message. Take the message. Thank the caller.\nPress [STATUS/CLEAR] -Disconnects the call. Review message before filing.\nDocument in the message *N/A (no answer) in the \"For\" field and in call notes\nPress [FILE]\nOn Some accounts you may see \"LWTCAS\" or \"TVP MSG\" for the dispatch instructions.\nLWTCAS (Leave Word to Call Answering Service) \nIf the call you are trying to patch goes to voicemail you the operator leave a message on the Client\u0027s voicemail stating as such:\n\"Please call the answering service you have a message, Thank you.\" \n(On some accounts you may have to leave a call back number, account will state if so and which number to leave.)\nPress [STATUS/CLEAR] \n-disconnects the outbound call/brings the caller back on\nAdvise the caller that the person they are trying to reach is not available and offer to take a message. Take the message. Thank the caller. \nPress [STATUS/CLEAR] -disconnects the call."},{"id":"Manual_Part_29","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 29 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Review message and document in the message ticket *LWTCAS in the \"For\" field and in the message ticket, at the end of the message.\n[FILE] the message. The Client will call the answering service and retrieve their message.\n*NOTE FOR MEDICAL ACCOUNTS If the instructions say Patch to Dr. O/C, which means Announce Patch. Always Announce Patch if it says to Patch to the Dr. O/C\nTVP MSG (Tone Voice Page Message) \nIf the call you are trying to patch goes to voicemail, leave a voicemail with all the callers information. (Make sure you open a message ticket and take down the caller’s information that the account requests prior to leaving the voicemail.\nOtherwise, you will not have the necessary information to leave on the voice mail for the Client.\nAfter Leaving entire voicemail\nPress [STATUS/CLEAR] - disconnects the outbound call/bring the caller back on\nAdvise the caller, that the person they are trying to reach is not available and you will let the Client know that they called.\nPress [STATUS/CLEAR] -disconnects the call. \nReview message and document in the message ticket *TVP MSG in the \"For\" field and in the call, at the end of the message. \n[FILE] the message.\nDUAL PATCHING\nDual Patching is used when the OPERATOR fails to PATCH OR ANNOUNCE PATCH the caller to the ON CALL. The OPERATOR must bring the CALLER back on the line and connect the CALLER to the ON CALL.\nPress DIAL key\nSelect a line from the TALK lines, enter the caller’s phone number (remember to add 1+to area codes outside of 602, 623 and 480)\nPress DIAL key, call will connect to caller.\nExample of what to say to caller: “Hello, this is the answering service, is this (confirm caller’s name) I’m going to connect you to the ON CALL, please stay on the line."},{"id":"Manual_Part_30","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 30 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Place the caller on PRIORITY HOLD by pressing ALT and CTRL keys.\nPress DIAL key, select a Talk line, select ON CALL’S contact number ON CALL’s page.\nAnnounce caller to the ON CALL “Dr (name) this is the answering service, I have (name of person or patient on the line, may I connect?” (ON CALL may ask for more information) Thank you I’ll connect.\nPress the PATCH key twice and then the STATUS CLEAR key to end the call.\nEnter *PATCHED in FOR FIELD and *SIDE DOCUMENTATION at bottom of message ticket: *PATCHED\nIf NO ANSWER, enter *No Answer or if you left VOICE MAIL for ON CALL to call back enter in FOR FIELD “LWTCAS” and at end of BODY of the MESSAGE.\nMEDICAL ACCOUNT INFORMATION\nHEALTH INSURANCE PORTABILITY AND ACCOUNTABILITY ACT OF 1996 (HIPPA): This is a federal law created to protect sensitive patient health information from being disclosed without the patient’s consent or knowledge. Answer Arizona adheres to this Privacy Rule. Answer Arizona employees are expected to follow this federal law by following the confidentiality of all patient information. Patient names, medical issues, and other personal information are not to be discussed. To do so will require disciplinary action.\nEMERGENCIES – ALL ER CALLS ARE TO BE PASSED TO THE ON-CALL DOCTOR OR NURSE. \nWhen you ask a caller if the call is an emergency, and they are unsure or say, “do not know.” Ask them “do you need me to contact the on-call physician now or can you wait for office to open?” In most cases the caller is uncertain and expects you to decide. However, we are not trained in the medical field. If the caller does need a call back, then put “yes” on Emergency otherwise the call will not be passed. Exceptions: \nIf someone in the same office is requesting a specific person to be paged"},{"id":"Manual_Part_31","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 31 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"If any personal calls such as family members\nA patient told by the doctor to have her/him paged.\nIf the on-call doctor requests a message be passed to someone else in his/her office.\nFamily members ask to speak to patient’s doctor: If patient is admitted into the hospital tell caller to ask nurse or med staff member to page patient’s doctor. Doctors can’t discuss patient’s medical information on the phone due to HIPPA laws. Doctor won’t know the hospital doctor’s orders until he talks directly to the medical staff. \nTake all early morning, next day surgery cancellations and same day surgery cancellations.\nREFER ROUTINE MESSAGES TO MEDICAL OFFICE: \nLab results, appointments, prescription refills. \nThe doctor left a message on the caller’s answering machine to call the office.\nReferrals \nForgot appointment time or need office directions.\nBilling questions.\nSAME DAY APPOINTMENT CANCELLATIONS OR EARLY MORNING SURGERY ``\n.CANCELLATIONS\nTake same day cancellations from patients up to 2 hours from when office opens (if opens at 8am, can take cancellations up to 10am).\nMessage Ticket information needed for medical cancellations: (1) Name (2) Phone number (3) Date of birth (4) Patient’s doctor (5) Re: Canceling (time of appointment at 7:30am/date) and (6) reason for canceling.\nAlways take early morning surgery cancellations as a courtesy to let surgeons know so they won’t show up at surgery site.\nTake same day cancellations from patients up to 2 hours from when office opens (if opens at 8am, can take cancellations up to 10am)\nPay attention to medical accounts that have different cancellation directions.\nOtherwise, refer callers ROUTINE OFFICE (Call back during normal business hours.\n(SHOW CXL TICKET EXAMPLE)"},{"id":"Manual_Part_32","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 32 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"PRESCRIPTIONS: Become familiar with medical accounts that have special instructions on after hour prescription (RX). There may be circumstances where an account says, “no RX” and the call is regarding medication for heart, seizures, blood pressure or diabetes. Then, take a message for the symptom of the drug, not the prescription request. \nSome doctors’ offices do not accept after-hour prescription requests AT ALL.\nOr may even say on the account “do not page on call with symptoms.”\nOffices may only accept emergency prescriptions but no routine refills after hours. \nOnly take prescription calls from the pharmacy if the pharmacy calls the answering service and request the doctor ON CALL be paged and it’s an urgent prescription.\nOffices may accept after-hour prescription requests if the office failed to call in the prescription, if they told the patient they would, or the prescriptions are for seizures, blood pressure, heart medication or diabetes. \nPrescription request if patient had recent surgery. \nOr if the patient is having a medication reaction and needs a replacement. \nWe are not trained in the medical field, but we do know what is urgent and can be life threatening if not taken regularly. Use your discretion and common sense. \nMEDICAL NAMES, LAB VALUES, TEST RESULTS: Do not take medication names (you may ask the caller what the medication is used for instead), do not take lab values or test results unless the account specifically states otherwise. Advise the caller that the doctor or medical staff in the doctor’s office will return the call. Note in the message RE: LAB VALUES, TEST RESULTS, MEDICATION.\nBACKLINE: Accounts may have a *BACKLINE. Never tell callers the account has a backline number."},{"id":"Manual_Part_33","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 33 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"MEDICAL OFFICES CLOSED: When medical offices are closed and the account indicates to refer routine calls to the office, tell the caller “For anything of a routine nature, the office prefers you to call back during office hours and they want us to only pass the emergency calls.\" If the caller insists on leaving a message, note this in the message. Try to get them to call back. You do not need to argue with the caller.\nMEDICAL ACCOUNTS -UNBLOCK TELEPHONE LINES\nAll medical accounts require us to ask callers to unblock their telephone line for them to receive a call back from a nurse or doctor O/C. To do so, please instruct them to enter *87 or *86 to unblock. \nHOSPITAL PAGE (PAGE THE ON CALL DOCTOR, NP, or PA): Ask for the following information on all hospital calls: Is the patient NEW or ESTABLISHED WITH THE DR? NEW means patient hasn’t had an office appointment. ESTABLISHED with the doctor means patient was seen in the office and a medical record established. New patients cannot use the AFTER-HOUR service, they must have been seen in the doctor’s office first. (Unless medical account information box says “New Patients OK”)\nHOSPITAL (PAGE) CALL: Obtain the following information from the caller on all PAGE calls: Always confirm with caller the call is for a PAGE not a CONSULT.\nIs this an ANNOUNCE PATCH account?\nCaller’s name (nurse or assistant or sometimes the doctor)\nHospital name (see hospital abbreviations) May also be a TRANSFER CENTER calling.\nPhone number, with extensions if available. ALWAYS CONFIRM the phone number with the caller. NEVER rely on the CALLER ID.\nPatient’s name – ALWAYS CONFIRM the spelling.\nDate of Birth, Room/Bed number, MRN# (Medical Records Number)"},{"id":"Manual_Part_34","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 34 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Patient’s Dr’s name. ALWAYS CONFIRM THE DR’S NAME ON THE ACCT, IF IT ISN’T, CHECK ACCT 0003 TO LOCATE THE DOCTORS FIRST AND LAST NAME AND ACCT OR ASK THE PATIENT/CALLER TO VERIFY THE OFFICE ADDRESS. \nNOTE: YOU CAN’T GET INTO THE DR’S DIRECTORY (0003) IF YOU HAVE AN ACTIVE TICKET ON THE SCREEN.\nLastly, ask the nature of the call. Use appropriate medical terms, i.e., buttocks, stool, urine etc.\nAgain, always verify name spelling, date of birth, hospital, room number, phone number. ALWAYS. \nEntering incorrect patient data information can delay urgent medical attention for the patient!\n HOSPITAL CONSULTS: One healthcare provider requests another healthcare provider from another hospital or medical office to review the patient’s medical history, examine the patient, and make recommendations as to care and treatment. Urgent Consults are paged to the ON CALL immediately. Routine consults (depending on time of day) will be paged out the next morning. Obtain the following information from the caller on all consults:\nIs this an ANNOUNCE PATCH account?\nPatient’s age and date of birth.\nRoom/bed number\nIs this patient new or established?\nWhich doctor is the consult for?\nName of doctor who is requesting the consultation.\nIs consult ROUTINE or URGENT? Enter the FOR field: *RTN CONSULT OR *URG CONSULT OR *STAT CONSULT.\nDIAGNOSIS (DX) OR REASON FOR THE CONSULT?\nInsurance\nMedical Records Number or MRN or MR#\nPEDIATRIC ACCOUNTS: \n7842 – Phoenix Children’s Pediatrics Tempe 2735 Scottsdale Pediatrics: No O/C, refer\n7844 – Phoenix Children’s Pediatrics Chandler 8804 – Estrella Pediatrics\n7845 – Phoenix Children’s Pediatrics Gilbert 3908 – St Joseph Pediatrics\n7846 – Phoenix Children’s Pediatrics SAN TAN 3411 – Phoenix Children’s Pediatrics Directory"},{"id":"Manual_Part_35","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 35 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"3433 – Desert Valley Pediatrics 3455 – West Valley Pediatrics\nValley Pediatrics Triage (VPT) – Website: https://pedstriage.phoenixchildrens.com (website, user name/password can be found on Account 3000)\nTake messages from callers calling to speak to the TRIAGE NURSE on the website VPT and put messages on the Spectrum Ticket during AFTER HOURS ONLY. \nTriage Nurse Account is ALWAYS sub-account .02 CAUTION! Do not put TRIAGE message ticket on HOME PAGE.\nRead SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS/LOCATE on times on the account when the TRIAGE NURSE is available.\nIf the caller doesn’t receive a CALL BACK in an hour, must do second call by re-entering information on the VPT website and NEW Spectrum Ticket with new encounter number.\nIf TRIAGE NURSE is calling to check in, transfer immediately to DISPATCHER.\nTriage nurse on call may call in stating she/he attempted a number of times to reach the caller with no answer, or no voice mail set up. You are to enter this information in the IF message (See Section IV page __) for instructions on completing an IF message or ask for help.\nNEWBORN NOTIFICATIONS: Hospitals will call the pediatric offices to report newborns. Most pediatric accounts have a page for Newborn Reporting. You must familiarize yourself with these calls. Take a “peek” at the NEWBORN page for pediatrics, familiarize yourself on how to get to this page on the accounts.\nIf Nurse says “Well baby, notify only (no call back) enter NEWBORN in FOR field.\n[SHOW WELL BABY MESSAGE TICKET]\nIf nurse says “Well baby, needs call back” enter in the FOR-field O/C.\n [SHOW NEED CALL BACK MESSAGE TICKET]\nName of caller/hospital, phone number (verify number)\n Baby Girl (BG) or Baby Boy (BB) Use abbreviations if need space for remaining information."},{"id":"Manual_Part_36","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 36 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Ask: Time born, weight, Apgar level (example: 9/9, 8/9, 7/9 6/9 etc.), who delivered, vaginal or c-section, well baby or sick baby, no call back needed (well but need call back) which doctor is assigned, room number (RM/#) or if no room number enter: RM/None\nUSING TABLES (UNDER CONSTRUCTION PENDING INSTRUCTIONS)\nTables provide different types of information to assist the operator in routing callers (customers of our clients) to the correct technician, doctor, realtor, property manager, etc. in a timely manner. \nTables will pop up when you click on the Hyperlink. [show a hyperlink]\nBelow are examples of accounts that utilize tables to assist us.\nACCOUNT TABLE: Use this table to locate correct account names and their account numbers. Must check “search” both the “Account Number or Name” and the Answer Phrase as there may be similar account names. Example: Arizona Digestive Health vs Arizona Digestive Phoenix Endoscopy. You can only search one at a time.\nonly \n“DRAFT”\nDOCTOR’S DIRECTORY ACCOUNT 0003 \nWhen taking messages from hospital or other medical facilities or from patients, we must verify the doctor is listed on the account. \nAsk the patient or hospital caller which doctor the patient sees.\nSearch the account for the doctor’s list (Accounts have a page for the doctor’s listing or doctor’s list may be on the HOME PAGE.)\nIf unable to locate the doctor’s name, you can search the DOCTOR’S DIRECTORY in Account 0003. (You cannot search this account if you have an active ticket on the screen. You must cancel the ticket first.)\nDoctor’s Directory is shown as a Table: \nRemove the black check mark in the small box.\nEnter the doctor’s last name, press search.\nA list of doctors with similar names will pop up with the account numbers they’re affiliated with."},{"id":"Manual_Part_37","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 37 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Select the correct first and last name of the doctor and the account number (confirm first this account is the same account the caller came in on) by DOUBLE CLICKING on the Table’s line. This will automatically connect you to the correct account.\nPull out a new message ticket and complete the ticket.\nIf the Doctor’s name is not listed, ask the caller to verify the Account’s address. If it matches, you can complete the message ticket. Add a SIDE DOCUMENTATION at bottom of message as follows: “*VERIFIED ADDRESS\n(See example of DOCTOR’S DIRECTORY TABLE – Account 0003 on next page)\nDoctor’s Directory Table – Account 0003\nMEDICAL TERMINOLOGY\nDR - Medical Doctor\nPA – Physician’s Assistant\nNP – Nurse Practitioner\nMW – Midwife\nMA – Medical Assistant\nEMT – Emergency Medical Technician\nPARAMEDICS – A person trained to give emergency medical care to people who are injured or ill.\nSTAT – Short term around Time or immediate response is needed.\nCRITICAL – Relating to a medical crisis or the value of a lab measurement.\nCODE BLUE – Hospital Emergency code used to describe the critical state of a patient. If a patient goes into cardiac arrest, respiratory or another emergency. The Rapid Response Team is always ready.\nSTEMI – ST Elevation Myocardial Infarction. Commonly known as a heart attack or when blood stops flowing properly to parts of the heart which injures the heart muscle due to lack of oxygen.\nMRN – Medical Records Number assigned to patients.\nAPGAR – Guideline used to check a newborn’s health. A-muscle tone, P-pulse, G-grimace/reflex irritability, A-appearance, R-respiration. On a scale of 9 to 1 (9 being the highest.)\nMEDICAL SPECIALITIES\nType of Practice\nHandles\nAllergy/Immunology\nAsthma/Sinus\nCardiovascular\nHeart and blood vessels\nDermatology\nSkin\nDiagnostic\nDiagnosis"},{"id":"Manual_Part_38","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 38 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Endocrinology\nGlands\nGastroenterology\nStomach, Intestines, Liver\nGeriatrics\nElderly\nHematology\nBlood disorders\nLaryngology\nThroat\nNeonatal\nNew Babies/Mothers\nNephrology\nKidneys\nNeurology\nNervous System\nObstetrics\nChildbirth\nOccupational Medicine\nWork related injuries\nOncology\nCancer\nOphthalmology\nEyes\nOtolaryngology\nEar, Nose, and throat\nOtology\nEar, Nose, and throat\nOrthopedics\nFoot, Bones, and joints\nPediatrics\nChildren and infants\nPodiatry\nFoot\nProctology\nColon and rectum\nPsychiatry\nMental Health\nPsychology\nCounselors\nPulmonary\nLungs\nRadiology\nX-rays\nRheumatology\nRheumatism/Arthritis\nThoracic\nChest/Lungs\nUrological\nUrinary Tract\n -DRAFT - HOSPITAL ABBREVIATIONS (ACCT 0004) 2023\nABRAZO ARROWHEAD\nABRAZO ARRWHD\nABRAZO MARYVALE\nABRAZO MV\nABRAZO CENTRAL\nABRAZO CTRL\nABRAZO SCOTTSDALE\nABRAZO SCTS\nABRAZO WEST\nABRAZO WST\nBANNER BAYWOOD\nBNR BAY\nBANNER BOSWELL\nBNR BOS\nBANNER DEL WEBB\nDEL WEBB\nBANNER DESERT\nBNR DES\nBANNER ESTRELLA\nBNR ESTRL\nBANNER GATEWAY\nBNR GTWY\nBANNER GOLDFIELD\nBNR GOLD\nBANNER HEART\nBNR HRT\nBANNER IRONWOOD\nBNR IRON\nBANNER MESA\nBNR MESA\nBANNER THUNDERBIRD\nBNR TBIRD\nBANNER UNIVERSITY PHOENIX\nBNR UNIV PHX\nCHANDLER REGIONAL\nCHNDLR REG\nDIGNITY HEALTH MEDICAL CENTER\nDHMC\nHEART VASCULAR INSTITUTE\nHVI\nHONOR HEALTH DEER VALLEY\nHH DV\nHONOR HEALTH NORTH MOUNTAIN\nHH NM\nHONOR HEALTH OSBORN\nHH OSB\nHONOR HEALTH SHEA\nHH SHEA\nHONOR HEALTH THOMPSON PEAK\nHH TPK\nHONOR HEALTH SONORAN CROSSING\nHH SC\nMERCY GILBERT\nMERCY GLBRT\nNORTON THORACIC INSTITUTE\nNTI\nPHOENIX CHILDREN’S HOSPITAL\nPCH\nST JOSEPH HOSPITAL\nST JOES\nVALLEY PEDIATRIC TRIAGE\nVPT\nDIGNITY HEALTH MEDICAL CENTER\nDHMG\nIN HOUSE MEMO’S\nIn-house memos are used to communicate between Answer Arizona staff for several reasons. Staff must sign on to Spectrum to generate a memo. Memos are sent from station to station."},{"id":"Manual_Part_39","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 39 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Reasons for sending memos: \nThe dispatcher is asking for clarification on a ticket you filed.\nDispatcher may request you to correct an incorrect ticket.\nThe operator may be asking you for help.\nGene or Ilene may have questions about payroll, leave request, etc.\nEntering/Delivering\nTo send a memo to another employee who is signed on to Spectrum.\nSpectrum screen must be cleared.\nSelect IF ENTER MSG\nEnter recipient’s name and station number (single digits add a “0” in front of the single digit).\nAt the bottom box enter your message.\nIf you use up the space in the message box and have additional information, file the first memo, and select a new memo to complete your message and file again.\nActing on a Memo to Another Operator\nMemos must be opened as soon as possible.\nOperator must alert the deliverer Memo was received or by alerting the sender you made corrects if dispatcher requested you correct a ticket.\nTransferring a Memo to Another Operator/Dispatcher\nYou may receive a memo in error. If it is intended for the dispatcher but an operator sent it to your station in error, you can transfer that memo to the dispatcher OR dispatcher may send a memo to all operators signed on by asking each operator who receives the MEMO to transfer it on to the next operator.\nTo TRANSFER a memo to another operator: Select TRANSFER on the Short Cut button and select the operator’s station number. Message is then transferred to the next operator.\nMISCELLANEOUS INSTRUCTIONS – Updated Draft\nThe following information pertains to basic situations only. There will be times when a judgment calls on your part will be necessary. Make yourself familiar with the guidelines. Some common situations are included below:"},{"id":"Manual_Part_40","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 40 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Do not refer to any information that is not listed on the account to be given; even if the caller is asking questions that you personally know the answers to. Only allowed to give out office phone numbers, fax numbers, and addresses. Ask if unsure! \nWE ARE A MESSAGE CENTER – DO NOT SAY YOU ARE THE ANSWERING SERVICE TOO MUCH. Callers are less likely to sound rude and annoyed if you follow this. \nDo not automatically say: “you are the message center” or quote the office hours. You may acknowledge if asked or if the caller continuously asks questions only office personnel could answer. Our clients pay us to take messages, NOT to tell the caller to call back when the office opens. Our services would not be needed if that were the case. Our clients would buy an answering machine for that type of service and save themselves money. Always offer to take a message unless it states on account to refer routine to office. \nOne of Answer Arizona’s standards is that no caller will ever be put on “automatic hold.” \nThis is when a caller does not get a chance to say anything before being put on hold. \nDO NOT SAY: “Good evening, Realty Executives, one moment please.” \nDO SAY: “Good evening, Honor Health Phoenix, can you hold, please?” See above for more instructions on page. \nRinging lines are your first priority. Answer them first, then go back to those holding. But never put a call on hold more than one time, unless traffic increases dramatically, then use priority hold. No one likes having to pick up an angry caller who has already given you information so if they give you the story keep them on priority hold."},{"id":"Manual_Part_41","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 41 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Once you enter anything into the body of a message (more than just who the caller asked for), that message is your responsibility. If you must put the caller on hold, use priority hold. Do not put them on regular hold for another operator to pick up. No one wants to try to finish taking a message someone else started. \nDue to the limited space available for a message, using abbreviations is necessary. A list of authorized in-house abbreviations has been included in this manual. Do not use any abbreviations for messages unless they are universally known or approved by Answer Arizona. \nThe dispatcher must be immediately by announcing aloud and making sure they acknowledge you, if call is either STAT, regarding a patient chest pains, Tempe School District Crisis Line-acct 2765-or regarding anyone stuck in an elevator. \nThe only calls that are to be transferred to a supervisor or dispatcher are calls that you cannot manage. Do not transfer or put calls on hold simply because the caller is difficult to understand or upset. Everyone gets their fair share of these types of calls. Not one person at Answer Arizona has the right to “pick and choose” which calls he/she will take. \nIf you have established that a call does need to be transferred to another operator, make sure the call is NOT put back on regular hold. Also notify the operator because the call was transferred to him/her by inputting a message in the message ticket. \nA “basic” message includes: \nName (first and last) with the spelling confirmed. If, when asked for a last name, the caller states he/she is a friend or relative, note that in the message. This will let our client know we are doing our job by asking. \nTelephone number (with area code). Verify EVERY number EVERY time!"},{"id":"Manual_Part_42","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 42 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Nature of the call (NOT just “please call”). If the caller refuses to say what the call is regarding or says our client will know, note that in the message. Our clients don’t pay us to just take a name and number, they like to know why a person is calling and could be more prepared if we take a complete message for when they call back. \nMany accounts request that the caller be asked if his/her call is an emergency. You must follow the account’s emergency criteria (if any). If a call indeed needs to be passed, even if it is not technically an emergency, you must mark it as an emergency, or it will be held for the office. \nEach account is different. Every time you answer the phone, look over the account, first hit the Trunk key then hit the Answer when ready, even if you are already familiar with that specific customer. Changes to the account may have taken place since the last time you answered on that account. Be sure to check out accounts 3400 (operator memos) and 4444(Answer Arizona’s office account) for any new operator memos every day before you start to answer the phone for your shift. \nSome accounts require specific information that is not included in a basic message. Any information out of the ordinary that our client requests us to get will be highlighted in blue. Any information out of the ordinary that our client requests that we refer to the callers is highlighted in green. Any important or urgent information will be highlighted in red."},{"id":"Manual_Part_43","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 43 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Most telephone numbers on accounts are unlisted and may not be referred to callers, such as backline numbers. Central office and fax numbers can always be referred to if they are listed. Any numbers the client has given us permission to refer to will be labeled as such. No other numbers may be referred at any time to callers. Backline numbers are used for emergency situations for the answering service to contact the office when they have their phones call forwarded. \nIf a caller is requesting a phone number for someone that is listed on the account, pass call the dispatch. They may refer to that number if the person requesting it is also listed on the account and can verify his/her own residence or pager number or mobile. You must transfer the call to the dispatcher on duty, who can access the numbers needed. \nFor any permanent changes to any account, refer to a caller to our business office M-F 8am-5pm. For example: new office staff, new home numbers, etc. You can take a temporary change and input it locate, but also notify management by inputting a message in account 4444 also. \nThere will be times when you will get an obscene caller. Simply try to take a message if they continue to be unruly or using obscene language notify the caller you can either take a message or if you need to put them on hold to calm down for a second or two. If the caller continues to use obscene language you may notify them, you disconnect the call. \nIN-HOUSE ABBREVIATIONS – ANSWER AZ APPROVED 2023\nAbbreviations Must Be Answer Arizona Approved \nOnly Use Abbreviations If Space Is Limited in Message Ticket\nADDRESS\nADDR\nOUT OF ORDER\nOOO\nADMITTANCE\nADMIT\nOUT OF TOWN\nOOT\nALPHA NUMERIC\nALPHA\nOUT TO LUNCH\nOTL\nANYONE\nAYO\nPAGE\nPG\nAPPOINTMENT\nAPPT\nPATIENT\nPT\nATTEMPTS REMAINING\nAR\nPICK UP\nP/U\nATTENTION"},{"id":"Manual_Part_44","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 44 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"ATTN\nPLEASE\nPLS\nATTORNEY\nATTY\nPREGNANT\nOB\nAUTHORIZATION\nAUTH\nPROBLEM\nPROB\nBACKLINE\nBKL\nPROPERTY\nPROP\nBEDROOM\nBDRM\nPULMONARY EMBOLISM\nPE\nBUILDING\nBLDG\nREFER\nREF\nCALL\nCL\nRESCHEDULE\nRESCHED\nCALL BACK\nCB OR C/B\nRESIDENCE\nRES\nCALL FORWARD\nC/F\nROOM\nRM\nCLOSED\nCLSD\nROUNDS\nRNDS\nCOMPANY\nCO\nROUTINE\nRTN\nDELIVERED\nDEL\nSESRVICE\nSVC\nDIGITAL PAGER\nDIG\nSUITE\nSTE\nDISCONNECTED\nDISCO\nSURGERY\nSX OR SURG\nDISTURBANCE\nDIST\nTELEPHONE\nTELE\nDO NOT GIVE OUT\nDNGO\nTELEPHONE ANS SVC\nTAS\nDO NOT REMOVE\nDNR\nTERM ID\nTID\nDIAGNOSIS\nDX\nTILL FURTHER NOTICE\nTFN\nEMERGENCY\nER\nTOMORROW\nTOM OR TOMR\nEMPLOYEE\nEMPL\nTONE ONLY PAGER\nTOP\nESTIMATE\nEST\nUNTIL\nTL\nEVENING\nEVE\nVALLEY PEDIATRICS TRIAGE\nVPT\nGONE FOR DAY\nGFD\nVOICE MAIL SYSTEM\nVMS\nGONE FOR WEEKEND\nGFWKND\nWILL CALL BACK\nWCB\nHANG UP\nHU\nWILL CALL IN\nWCI\nHOLD CALLS\nHLD CLS\nATTENDING ON CALL\nAOC\nHOURS\nHRS\nWILL CALL BACK\nWCB\nHISTORY\nHX\nWILL CALL IN\nWCI\nIF NO ANSWER\nINA\nATTENDING ON CALL\nAOC\nIMPORTANT\nIMPT\nMANAGEMENT\nMGMT\nINSURANCE\nINS\nNO ANSWER\nN/A\nINTERNAL MEDICINE\nIM\nLEFT WORD\nL/W\nLEFT WORD CALL ANS SVC\nLWTCAS\nOFFICE\nOFC\nON CALL\nO/C\nOPERATOR\nOPER\nCOMMONLY MISSPELLED WORDS 2023\nAbdominal\nEndoscopy\nPrivilege\nAbscess\nEntrepreneur\nProcedure\nAddendum\nEucalyptus\nReferral\nAetna Insurance\nExtinguisher\nRespiratory\nAHCCCS (access)\nExtremely\nRhythm\nAmnesia\nFeces\nSaguaro\nAnalytic\nFibrosis\nSegregate\nAnalyze\nGamma knife\nSeizure\nAnesthesia\nGangrene\nSubpoena\nApache\nHallucinate\nSuicidal\nAppendicitis\nHemorrhage\nSuicide\nAppraisal\nHemorrhoid\nSyncope\nAsthma\nHematuria\nTachycardia\nArrhythmia\nHematemesis\nThrombocytopenia\nAtrial Fibrillation (Afib)\nHyperglycemia\nThrombophlebitis\nBronchitis\nHypoxia\nTomorrow\nBradycardia\nHysterectomy\nTonsillectomy\nCardiac\nImpetigo\nTonsillitis\nCatheter\nIncision\nTroponin\nChemotherapy\nInfluenza\nTuberculosis\nCholelithiasis\nLegible\nUlcer\nCholecystic\nMastitis"},{"id":"Manual_Part_45","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 45 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Umbilical\nCholecystectomy\nMastectomy\nVandalism\nCholecystectomy\nMeningitis\nVenereal\nCirrhosis\nMetastatic\nVentricular\nCollege\nMississippi\nColonoscopy\nMissouri\nConcussion\nMitosis\nConjunctivitis\nMojave or Mohave\nConstipation\nMucus\nConsulate\nNausea\nConvenience\nNauseous\nCouncil (assembly)\nNecessary\nCounsel (advice)\nOperation\nCrohn’s\nPancreatic\nDeposition\nPancreatitis\nDiabetic\nPancytopenia\nDiabetes\nPsychiatry\nDiagnosis\nPsychiatric\nDiarrhea\nPhysiatrist\nEczema\nPneumonia\nEmphysema\nPrenatal\nGlossary of Terms used in an Answering Service\nAnnounce Patch: An announcement is made to client of who is on the line. In some cases, we need to announce callers name \u0026 information.\nAnswer Phrase: The actual words the customer instructs the operator to use when a client\u0027s line rings in. \"Thank you for calling Dr. Jones office, may I help you,\" is an example.\nApgar: A system for evaluating an infant’s physical condition at birth. (Heart rate, respiration, muscle tone, response to stimuli, and color are rated 1 minute then again at 5 minutes after birth)\nAuto Answer: A recorded message that can automatically put the caller on hold if all operators are busy.\nAutomatic Call Distribution: A computer answering system function which routes calls to available operators.\nBlocked line: A telephone feature available from most phone companies. The telephone line does not accept outside phone lines if they are BLOCKED. (TO UNBLOCK: *77) (TO BLOCK *87) (requires a 10 digit # in order to get the call to go through usually by pressing “000-000-0000”)\nCaller ID: Caller identification technology allows the recipient of a telephone call, when the phone rings, to learn the phone number or name of the caller before picking up the receiver."},{"id":"Manual_Part_46","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 46 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Call Transfer: Allows you to transfer a call from your phone to someone else\u0027s phone.\nCheck In: The client calls in to the messaging bureau to check for messages.\nCheck Out: The client calls to notify the messaging bureau that he will not be taking his own calls and that the message center is \"on.\"\nConference Call: A call consisting of a connection among three or more callers participating in a simultaneous discussion.\nConnect Time: The length of time a caller accesses the system. From the time the system comes off-hook to answer a ring signal, until the call ends and the line is back on-hook.\nDelivered Messages: Messages that have been passed/delivered to a client. [REDELVR]\nDirect Inward Dialing (DID): The ability for a caller outside a company to call an internal extension without having to pass through an operator or attendant. It is a special type of seven-digit number which can only receive calls. They can be purchased by messaging bureaus in blocks at very low cost. By assigning a unique DID number to each customer, and having the customer call forward to the number, the bureau can identify which client\u0027s call he is receiving.\nDown file: List of messages that have been delivered to a client. [UNDELV MSG]\nELI (Expanded Locate Instructions): \nFAX (Facsimile): FAX machines are telephone equipment which lets you send a copy of written or drawn material over the telephone to a receiving FAX.\nHard Copy: A printout, on paper, of information contained in the computer.\nHeadset: A telephone set worn on the head.\nHypertext Command: A target command that will allow you to either display another account, display a message ticket, or dial out."},{"id":"Manual_Part_47","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 47 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Internet: An unregulated, global confederation of computer networks linked through regional, private business and educational networks.\nMailbox: Message storage space provided to a user for storing messages.\nMailbox Number: Seven-digit number, or four-digit extension number assigned to a subscriber\u0027s message storage space.\nMessage Center: A service bureau consisting of live operators and/or an automated system recording and delivering messages.\nMLS Number: Real Estate agents list a number that is designated to a property address they have for sale.\nModem: Short for modulator-demodulator. Modems connect two separate computers via telephone by converting digital signals into analog signals enabling computers to send data over the telephone networks.\nOrder Entry: The action of recording an order from a caller for a new product or service.\nO/C Scheduler: Spectrum On-Call Scheduler tracks our client’s complex schedules so that messages can be relayed accurately, day and night. \nPager: A small device, sometimes called a beeper, which signals the person carrying it that the TAS has an important message.\nPatch: The connection of two parties at the messaging service switchboard.\nPrivate Branch Exchange (PBX): Customer premise equipment usually owned and operated by a single company with telephone lines to place or receive calls to the public network and communicate with other extensions within the system.\nPrompts: Audio message advising the user that the system is waiting for a command.\nRetained message: messages we keep in possession on the operator consoles 1-10 for 30 days.\nRing Count: On manual and computerized concentrator systems, the ring count is the client\u0027s instructions as to how quickly the call should be answered. A standard ring count is three.\nSMS:"},{"id":"Manual_Part_48","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 48 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Spectrum Secure Messaging:\nStexting:\nSpeed dial #: a number with a purple dot used for easy access to dial out /alpha page/email/display an account. a speed dialed number is a number preprogrammed in the computer allowing rapid dial while reducing errors in dialing.\nTAS: Telephone answering service.\nTiger Text: \nTraffic: The flow of calls (attempted and completed) across a telecommunications network.\nTranscription: Conversion of voice data into written text.\nTrunk: A telephone circuit or channel connecting two switching systems. (Between a telephone company central office and a TAS computerized answering service.)\nUndelivered: A list of messages that have NOT been passed. [DELIVER MSG]\nUpfile: A list where messages that have not been passed and are waiting to be delivered. [DELIVER MSG]\nVoice Mail: A specific voice messaging service in which users record and distribute messages among other subscribers, each of whom has a unique voice mailbox or address.   -622300- Press “C” to Cancel Message\n00Press “C” to Cancel Message\n-622300- TALK\n4\n00TALK\n4\n-622300- TALK\n3\n00TALK\n3\n-622300- TALK\n2\n00TALK\n2\n-622300- TALK\n1\n00TALK\n1\n-622300- XFER\n3333\n00XFER\n3333\n-622300- \n00\n-622300- \n00\n-622300- \n00\n-622300- \n00\n-622300- \n00\n-622300- \n00\nHOW TO USE ACCOUNTS: 0000, 3000, 3400, 4000, 4444.07 \nAccount #0000: Is the Employee account where shift times, break times, and in-house messages can be accessed.\nAccount #0003: Is the Doctor’s Directory. This includes all Answer Arizona Medical Accounts. This directory is set up following the TABLES format. You must remove the black checkmark before searching a doctor’s name.\n[INSERT example of the doctor’s table]"},{"id":"Manual_Part_49","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 49 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"Account 3000: Is the Nurses/Triage account where you can find the Pediatric Accounts and the Triage Sub-Accounts that includes the Valley Pediatrics Triage (VPT), Username and Password. [NEEDS MORE INFORMATION]\nAccount 3400: Is where messages are posted regarding account changes, client complaints, etc. This account must be checked at or during dispatcher’s/operator’s shift. Each of us must read the account changes or account complaints and INTIAL and DATE that we have read the information. \nAccount 4444.07: Is where you can “FIX” your timecard or request TIME OFF. Read the Requesting Time Off GUIDELINES before requesting time off. \nDRAFT UPON APPROVAL TO INCLUDE\nCONTACT ANSWER ARIZONA PHONE NUMBERS\nAnswer Arizona – Use this number to notify dispatcher you will be late or calling out.\nCalling out – Use this number to notify Gene Burger you are calling out: 480-818-0702\nDraft Upon Approval and Any Additions/Deletions for This Section\nSPECTRUM SYSTEM TROUBLE SHOOT\n(Requested TD to contribute to this Section and Will Add the instructions from 5083 regarding if having system issues)\nTIGER CONNECT WEBSITE\nPMD WEBSITE\nADP TIME SHEET – Signing in and Out\nVPN – VIRTUAL PRIVATE NETWORK: Allows employees to access their company’s private network when working from home. It is very important to LOG OFF the VPN when done with your shift. Otherwise, other operators attempting to sign on at their shift times after you will not be able to do so. \nIf you don’t sign off the VPN, it may take the IT person an hour to access your equipment to log off for you. \n*REMEMBER TO SIGN OFF THE VPN AT THE END OF YOUR SHIFT*\nIf the system is “off-line” or in “retry,” and the screens are not functioning, you should still be able to take messages."},{"id":"Manual_Part_50","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 50 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"The messages must be handwritten on paper and entered into the accounts once the system is back online. \nAnswer the phone by saying “Good morning/evening, this is ___, may I help you?” (Only answer this way if the information screens are not being displayed).\nWrite down the account number, which will appear in the “talk” window. \nIf you take an emergency call, alert the dispatcher immediately. If callers/clients, ask questions just refer to them we are currently updating our system sorry for the inconvenience. \nThis section is recommended, pending Answer Arizona’s Approval\nMILITARY ALPHABET: History of and Reason for Using\nThe Military Alphabet is a special phonetic alphabet used by the military to communicate over radios and other devices. The military alphabet was created to improve communication among military members.\nIt is a set of twenty-six words that are used to spell out letters when communicating over the radio or telephone. \nThis system helps to ensure clarity and accuracy in communication, especially in noisy or difficult environments. The military alphabet consists of the standard English alphabet, plus extra words that are specific to military use which include words “alpha,” “bravo,” and ‘Charlie.”\nThis alphabet is used anywhere that clear audio communication is of the highest importance, such as Answer Arizona who takes medical emergency messages where accuracy of names and medical terms is crucial. \nUse the Military alphabet to accurately confirm the spelling of names and medical terms:\nExample: Confirm spelling of ARIZONA using the following alphabet by spelling out the letters using the military alphabet to confirm the letter:\nA\nALPHA\nN\nNOVEMBER\nB\nBRAVO\nO\nOSCAR\nC\nCHARLIE\nP\nPAPA\nD\nDELTA\nQ\nQUEBEC\nE\nECHO\nR\nROMEO\nF\nFOXTROT\nS\nSIERRA\nG\nGOLF\nT\nTANGO\nH\nHOTEL"},{"id":"Manual_Part_51","title":"Employee Training Manual - Part 51 of 51","url":"Revised%20Spectrum%20Manual%20-%20July%202023.pdf","text":"U\nUNIFORM\nI\nINDIA\nV\nVICTOR\nJ\nJULIET\nW\nWHISKEY\nK\nKILO\nX\nXRAY\nL\nLIMA\nY\nYANKEE\nM\nMIKE\nZ\nZULU\nA – ALPHA\nR – ROMEO\nI – INDIA\nZ – ZULU\nO- OSCAR\nN- NOVEMBER\nA - ALPHA"},{"id":"SOP_01_Answer_Hold_Transfer","title":"Answering, Holding \u0026 Transferring Calls","url":"SOP_01_Answer_Hold_Transfer.html","text":"Answering, Holding \u0026 Transferring Calls \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Answering, Holding \u0026 Transferring Calls\n Step-by-step Spectrum procedure for answering a call, using Universal or Priority Hold, and transferring calls between consoles.\n SOP ID SOP-01\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Manual Area Incoming Calls / Hold / Transfer\n Purpose\n Use this procedure to answer incoming calls in Spectrum, place callers on Universal or Priority Hold correctly, and transfer a caller to another agent console.\n Core rule: The caller is not live when you first select a ringing TALK line. Press ANSWER to bring the caller live.\n Visual Workflow\n RING on TALK line\n →\n Select TALK 1–4\n →\n Press ANSWER\n →\n Handle / Hold / Transfer\n →\n CLEAR when finished\n Procedure A — Answer an Incoming Call\n 1\n Select the ringing line\n Press the corresponding TALK 1–4 key. Spectrum displays the account screen; the caller is not live yet.\n TALK 1–4 \n 2\n Bring the caller live\n Press ANSWER .\n ANSWER \n 3\n Use the required professional phrasing\n “May I ask who is calling, please?”\n The manual requires professional, polite, courteous wording and use of “please” and “thank you.”\n 4\n Disconnect when complete\n Press CLEAR after the call is complete.\n CLEAR \n Procedure B — Universal Hold\n Universal Hold makes the call available for pickup by all agents.\n 1\n Ask permission\n “Can you hold, please.”\n The manual also gives a modified account answer phrase: “Benjamin Franklin, this is ___ May I Place You on Hold?”\n 2\n If the caller agrees\n Say “Thank you,” then press HOLD . The TALK key changes to a red HOLD state.\n HOLD \n 3\n If the caller declines\n Do not put the caller on hold. Take the call. If it is an account you are not trained to manage, tell the caller you will transfer them to someone who can assist.\n Procedure C — Priority Hold\n Priority Hold is exclusive to the agent who initiated it. The manual states a console can have up to four Priority Holds or transferred calls at once and instructs operators not to place the same caller on Priority Hold more than two times during the same call.\n Current caller\n →\n SHIFT + HOLD\n or ALT + HOLD \n →\n PHLD — exclusive to your console\n Procedure D — Transfer to Another Console\n 1\n Start transfer\n Press ALT + T or choose the Transfer shortcut button.\n ALT + T \n 2\n Enter the station number\n Type the destination console. For a single-digit station, add a leading zero: Console 2 = 02 ; Console 22 = 22 .\n Receiving a Transferred Call\n Action What it does \n Press the corresponding TALK key once Selects the XFER call and opens the account screen; caller is not live yet. \n Press ANSWER Brings the transferred caller live. \n Alternative Press the corresponding TALK key a second time to bring the caller live. \n Required Call Phrases\n Situation Manual phrase \n Opening “May I ask who is calling, please?” \n Putting on hold “Can you hold, please.” \n Returning from hold “Thank you for waiting. May I help you?” \n Patch release “One moment please while I connect you to __ (client’s name) __.” \n Operator Check\n I selected the correct TALK line before pressing ANSWER.\n I asked permission before placing a caller on hold.\n I used Universal vs. Priority Hold intentionally.\n I used a two-digit station number when transferring.\n I used professional “please” and “thank you” phrasing.\nThis SOP is a visual job aid derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Account-specific instructions, Special Locate information, Active Alerts, and dispatcher direction take precedence when the manual says an account may have exceptions."},{"id":"SOP_02_Message_Tickets","title":"Creating \u0026 Documenting Message Tickets","url":"SOP_02_Message_Tickets.html","text":"Creating \u0026 Documenting Message Tickets \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Creating \u0026 Documenting Message Tickets\n A visual SOP for opening, completing, reviewing, documenting, editing, and filing Spectrum message tickets.\n SOP ID SOP-02\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Manual Area Types of Messages / Message Ticket Documentation\n Purpose\n Use this procedure to create, complete, document, review, and file Spectrum message tickets accurately. This SOP also distinguishes ordinary message tickets, Announce Patch tickets, and Patch calls.\n Accuracy is mandatory. The manual states that confirmation of numbers, addresses, and names is mandatory because unclear or incorrect messages can delay assistance.\n Visual Workflow\n Read account instructions\n →\n IF / ENTER MSG\n →\n Collect requested information\n →\n Set ER + FOR fields\n →\n Review\n →\n FILE\n Procedure A — Create a Standard Message Ticket\n 1\n Check account instructions first\n Read the Information screens and follow the order requested by the account. Use Page Up or Page Down to review additional information pages.\n 2\n Open the message ticket\n Press IF/ENTER MSG .\n IF / ENTER MSG \n 3\n Collect and enter the caller\u0027s information\n Follow the exact field order requested by the account. For two-page tickets, press TAB to move to the next page.\n TAB \n 4\n Mark routing information\n Where applicable, mark the ER field Y or N and enter Ofc or O/C in the FOR field so the dispatcher knows whether to hold or pass the message.\n 5\n Review before filing\n Verify names, phone numbers, addresses, spelling, and the reason for the call. Write clearly and include who, what, when, and where.\n 6\n File the ticket\n Press FILE when the ticket is complete.\n FILE \n Writing Standard\n Requirement Manual guidance \n Voice Write in first person as if the caller is writing the message: I, we, me, mine, my, our. \n Clarity Use accurate grammar, correct spelling, and wording that is easy for the dispatcher/on-call/nurse to understand. \n Completeness Include relevant who, what, when, and where details. \n Verification Confirm names, telephone numbers, and addresses. \n Procedure B — Announce Patch Ticket\n Announce Patch requires a ticket. Open the message ticket and collect the account-requested information before Announce Patching.\n Open ticket\n →\n Collect caller information\n →\n Announce Patch\n →\n Document *Patched / result\n →\n FILE\n Patching directions may appear in the Special Locate , On-Call Scheduler , Expanded Locate , or account Information screens.\n Procedure C — Patch Calls\n Patch calls do not require a completed message ticket. The manual instructs the operator to simply patch the caller to the client.\n Side Documentation Examples\n Code Meaning \n *C/B MISSED CALL Call back missed call \n *N/A No answer \n *BKL NO ANSWR Backline no answer \n *VM FULL Unable to leave voicemail; voicemail full \n *CLR INSISTS ER Caller insists emergency \n *2ND, 3RD CL Second or third call \n *CANCEL MESSAGE Cancellation \n *PATCHED Caller was patched \n Editing, Second Calls, and Cancellations\n Manual note: the Copy/Save section is marked “SECTION BEING UPDATED.” Follow current supervisor/dispatcher direction if local practice differs.\n Use SAVE to edit an undelivered message or place a message on the Incomplete stack.\n Press FILE after edits are complete.\n For a second or third call or a cancellation, the manual instructs creating a new ticket and adding side documentation such as *2ND, *3RD, or CANCEL.\n On a second call, always reconfirm the caller\u0027s phone number.\n Do not allow STAT/STEMI/ASAP-type calls to sit in the Incomplete stack; finish the ticket and alert the dispatcher.\n Operator Check\n I read the account instructions before entering the ticket.\n I verified all names and numbers with the caller.\n I used the correct ER and FOR routing fields where required.\n I documented exceptions/patch results with side documentation.\n I reviewed the ticket before pressing FILE.\nThis SOP is a visual job aid derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Account-specific instructions, Special Locate information, Active Alerts, and dispatcher direction take precedence when the manual says an account may have exceptions."},{"id":"SOP_03_Office_Checkout_OnCall","title":"Office Check-Out, On-Call \u0026 Special Locate Updates","url":"SOP_03_Office_Checkout_OnCall.html","text":"Office Check-Out, On-Call \u0026 Special Locate Updates \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Office Check-Out, On-Call \u0026 Special Locate Updates\n Procedure for office forwarding/check-out calls, collecting on-call information, updating Special Locate, and notifying the dispatcher.\n SOP ID SOP-03\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Manual Area Office Check-Out / Special Locate / On-Call\n Purpose\n Use this procedure when an office calls to say its phones are being forwarded, the office is leaving for lunch/a meeting/the day/weekend, or the client provides on-call instructions that must be documented in Special Locate and communicated to the dispatcher.\n Before placing an office caller on hold: the manual instructs operators to look at Caller ID because most offices can be identified by it.\n Visual Workflow\n Office calls in\n →\n Identify checkout/forwarding status\n →\n Collect return + O/C details\n →\n Update Special Locate\n →\n Notify dispatcher\n Common Office Check-Out Language\n What the client may say Manual shorthand / action \n “Stepping out for lunch.” OTL \n “Going into a meeting.” C/F IN MTG TL [time] \n “We are forwarding the phones.” / “We are rolling the phones.” / “You have our phones.” Document forwarding status and any time/on-call instructions provided. \n “Leaving for the day/weekend.” GFD or GFWKND; update Special Locate accordingly. \n Procedure A — Handle the Office Check-Out\n 1\n Identify the office\n Check Caller ID before placing the call on hold.\n 2\n Clarify the forwarding/check-out status\n Determine whether the office is stepping out temporarily, going into a meeting, forwarding phones, or leaving for the day/weekend.\n 3\n Get the time frame\n Ask when the office will return or how long the temporary instruction is in effect, if the client provides or needs to provide a time frame.\n 4\n Ask for call-handling instructions\n The office may give instructions for emergency versus routine calls and may identify who is on call.\n Procedure B — Collect On-Call Information\n When the office provides on-call information, the manual says always obtain:\n Name of the person, technician, or doctor on call.\n Start and end date/time for the on-call assignment.\n Name of the client who provided the on-call information.\n If the instructions are in-depth or confusing: alert the dispatcher. The manual says the dispatcher may have you transfer the client to them. Tell the client you will transfer them to the dispatcher who can better assist; the manual specifically says not to say “HOLD.”\n Procedure C — Update Special Locate\n The Special Locate contains short-term account information. The manual repeatedly stresses that operators must read it when taking calls because it can contain temporary patching, emergency, office-closure, and on-call instructions.\n 1\n Open Locate Edit\n Answer a call or display the account, then press DELETE/LOCATE EDIT .\n LOCATE EDIT \n 2\n Enter the current information\n Document the office status/on-call instruction in the approved short format.\n 3\n File the update\n Press FILE . The manual notes the border will appear purple after the update.\n FILE \n On-Call Locate Formats from the Manual\n Situation Format \n Medical on-call DR (name) O/C TL (date) \n Doctor from another account DR (name) O/C TL (date) * DISPLAY ACCT (number)*** \n Refer another doctor\u0027s office number DR (name) O/C TL (date) ***REFER (office number)*** \n Other on-call (name) O/C TL (date) or O/C: (name) TL (date) \n Backup B/U: (name) TL (date) \n Medical verification rule: the manual says to verify the doctor is listed with contact information on screen. If the doctor is not listed, ask a dispatcher before disconnecting with the client. It also says never give out phone numbers unless the account clearly says “REFER” or “MGO.”\n Dispatcher Notification\n Whenever the office gives on-call instructions, notify the dispatcher of what the client advised and document those instructions in Special Locate.\n Every-Call Locate Habit\n Answer call\n →\n Look at SPECIAL LOCATE\n →\n Follow temporary instructions\n The manual warns that failing to follow Special Locate instructions can delay an emergency call-out.\n Operator Check\n I checked Caller ID before placing an office caller on hold.\n I captured who is on call, the effective dates/times, and who provided the information.\n I documented the current instruction in Special Locate.\n I informed the dispatcher of the on-call instructions.\n I escalated confusing or incomplete instructions before disconnecting the client.\nThis SOP is a visual job aid derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Account-specific instructions, Special Locate information, Active Alerts, and dispatcher direction take precedence when the manual says an account may have exceptions."},{"id":"SOP01","title":"Sign On to the Agent Console","url":"SOP_Library/SOP01.html","text":"Sign On to the Agent Console | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Sign On to the Agent Console\n Sign on to the Spectrum Agent Console from the Idle state.\n SOP ID SOP-01\n Manual Section GETTING STARTED\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Sign on to the Spectrum Agent Console from the Idle state.\n Visual Workflow\n Start from Idle\n →\n Initiate sign-on\n →\n Complete validation\n Procedure\n 1\n Start from Idle\n Confirm the console is in the Idle state.\n 2\n Initiate sign-on\n Press SN ON on the numeric keypad, or use the On/Off shortcut with the mouse.\n SN ON \n 3\n Complete validation\n Complete the sign-on validation presented by Spectrum.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Start from Idle.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Initiate sign-on.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Complete validation.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP02","title":"View Operator Statistics","url":"SOP_Library/SOP02.html","text":"View Operator Statistics | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n View Operator Statistics\n View your current-session call statistics while signed on.\n SOP ID SOP-02\n Manual Section OPERATOR INFORMATION\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n View your current-session call statistics while signed on.\n Visual Workflow\n Open statistics\n →\n Review the Operator Information window\n →\n Close statistics\n Procedure\n 1\n Open statistics\n Press Apps + O, or click the Stats Agent Shortcut button.\n Apps + O \n 2\n Review the Operator Information window\n Review the call statistics accumulated since sign-on.\n 3\n Close statistics\n Click Close or press SELECT.\n SELECT \n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Open statistics.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Review the Operator Information window.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Close statistics.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP03","title":"Sign Off and Transfer Pending Work","url":"SOP_Library/SOP03.html","text":"Sign Off and Transfer Pending Work | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Sign Off and Transfer Pending Work\n Sign off Spectrum correctly and transfer pending pages, memos, or reminders before leaving.\n SOP ID SOP-03\n Manual Section SIGNING OFF and Assigning Work FROM THE CONSOLE\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Sign off Spectrum correctly and transfer pending pages, memos, or reminders before leaving.\n Visual Workflow\n Start sign-off\n →\n Validate sign-off\n →\n Check pending work\n →\n Transfer pending work\n Procedure\n 1\n Start sign-off\n Press SN OFF or click the On/Off shortcut.\n SN OFF \n 2\n Validate sign-off\n At the Sign-Off prompt, type Y.\n 3\n Check pending work\n If pending work exists, choose the dispatcher\u0027s station number from the list.\n 4\n Transfer pending work\n Select Transfer so pending pages, transmit memos, and reminders move to the selected console.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Start sign-off.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Validate sign-off.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Check pending work.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Transfer pending work.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP04","title":"Display a Master Account","url":"SOP_Library/SOP04.html","text":"Display a Master Account | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Display a Master Account\n Display a four-digit master account from Standby.\n SOP ID SOP-04\n Manual Section DISPLAYING AN ACCOUNT OR SUB-ACCOUNT\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Display a four-digit master account from Standby.\n The manual notes that Down Arrow moves to the next sequential master or sub-account; Right Arrow moves to the next sequential master while bypassing sub-accounts.\n Visual Workflow\n Start from Standby\n →\n Press DISPLAY\n →\n Enter the account\n Procedure\n 1\n Start from Standby\n Make sure Spectrum is in Standby.\n 2\n Press DISPLAY\n Press DISPLAY on the numeric keypad.\n DISPLAY \n 3\n Enter the account\n Enter the four-digit master account number.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Start from Standby.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Press DISPLAY.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Enter the account.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP05","title":"Display a Sub-Account","url":"SOP_Library/SOP05.html","text":"Display a Sub-Account | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Display a Sub-Account\n Open a one- or two-digit sub-account while viewing its master account.\n SOP ID SOP-05\n Manual Section DISPLAYING AN ACCOUNT OR SUB-ACCOUNT\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Open a one- or two-digit sub-account while viewing its master account.\n Visual Workflow\n Display the master account\n →\n Press DISPLAY\n →\n Enter sub-account number\n →\n Select it\n Procedure\n 1\n Display the master account\n Begin on the appropriate master account.\n 2\n Press DISPLAY\n Press DISPLAY.\n DISPLAY \n 3\n Enter sub-account number\n Enter the one- or two-digit sub-account number.\n 4\n Select it\n Press SELECT to move to the sub-account.\n SELECT \n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Display the master account.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Press DISPLAY.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Enter sub-account number.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Select it.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP06","title":"Return from a Sub-Account","url":"SOP_Library/SOP06.html","text":"Return from a Sub-Account | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Return from a Sub-Account\n Return from a sub-account to the main or master account screen.\n SOP ID SOP-06\n Manual Section DISPLAYING AN ACCOUNT OR SUB-ACCOUNT\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Return from a sub-account to the main or master account screen.\n Visual Workflow\n Choose destination\n →\n Return to main screen\n →\n Return to master account\n Procedure\n 1\n Choose destination\n Decide whether you need the main screen or main master-account screen.\n 2\n Return to main screen\n Press DISPLAY + SELECT when in a sub-account.\n DISPLAY + SELECT \n 3\n Return to master account\n Press DISPLAY + HOME for the main master-account screen.\n DISPLAY + HOME \n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Choose destination.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Return to main screen.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Return to master account.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP07","title":"Search for an Account","url":"SOP_Library/SOP07.html","text":"Search for an Account | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Search for an Account\n Search Spectrum by account name or keyword.\n SOP ID SOP-07\n Manual Section Displaying accounts and Locate instructions\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Search Spectrum by account name or keyword.\n Visual Workflow\n Open account search\n →\n Enter search text\n →\n Select the correct result\n Procedure\n 1\n Open account search\n Press ALT + S or click ACCOUNTS in the menu.\n ALT + S \n 2\n Enter search text\n Type the account name or a relevant keyword in the search bar.\n 3\n Select the correct result\n Open the intended account and verify it before handling the call.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Open account search.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Enter search text.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Select the correct result.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP08","title":"Answer an Incoming Call","url":"SOP_Library/SOP08.html","text":"Answer an Incoming Call | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Answer an Incoming Call\n Select a ringing call, bring the caller live, and disconnect when complete.\n SOP ID SOP-08\n Manual Section INCOMING CALLS — ANSWERING A CALL\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Select a ringing call, bring the caller live, and disconnect when complete.\n Visual Workflow\n Select the call\n →\n Bring caller live\n →\n Handle the call\n →\n Disconnect\n Procedure\n 1\n Select the call\n Press the TALK 1–4 key that corresponds to the ringing call. The account screen opens, but the caller is not live.\n TALK 1–4 \n 2\n Bring caller live\n Press ANSWER.\n ANSWER \n 3\n Handle the call\n Follow the account instructions and required call phrases.\n 4\n Disconnect\n Press CLEAR when the call is complete.\n CLEAR \n Suggested / Required Phrase\n May I ask who is calling, please?\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Select the call.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Bring caller live.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Handle the call.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Disconnect.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP09","title":"Place a Caller on Universal Hold","url":"SOP_Library/SOP09.html","text":"Place a Caller on Universal Hold | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Place a Caller on Universal Hold\n Place a caller on a hold that can be picked up by all agents.\n SOP ID SOP-09\n Manual Section PLACING A CALL ON UNIVERSAL HOLD\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Place a caller on a hold that can be picked up by all agents.\n If the caller says no, do not place them on hold; take the call. The manual says not to put callers on automatic hold.\n Visual Workflow\n Ask permission\n →\n If caller agrees\n →\n Confirm hold state\n →\n Return appropriately\n Procedure\n 1\n Ask permission\n Ask the caller if they can hold.\n 2\n If caller agrees\n Say thank you and press HOLD.\n HOLD \n 3\n Confirm hold state\n The TALK key changes to a red HOLD state.\n 4\n Return appropriately\n When returning, thank the caller for waiting.\n Suggested / Required Phrase\n Can you hold, please.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Ask permission.\n Complete step 2 correctly: If caller agrees.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Confirm hold state.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Return appropriately.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP10","title":"Place a Caller on Priority Hold","url":"SOP_Library/SOP10.html","text":"Place a Caller on Priority Hold | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Place a Caller on Priority Hold\n Place a call on hold exclusively for the agent who initiated the hold.\n SOP ID SOP-10\n Manual Section PLACING A CALL ON PRIORITY HOLD\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Place a call on hold exclusively for the agent who initiated the hold.\n The manual states a console can have up to four Priority Holds or transferred calls at once and says not to place the same caller on Priority Hold more than two times during the same call.\n Visual Workflow\n Identify the need\n →\n Place Priority Hold\n →\n Resume the same caller\n Procedure\n 1\n Identify the need\n Use Priority Hold when the call should remain exclusive to your console.\n 2\n Place Priority Hold\n Press SHIFT + HOLD or ALT + HOLD.\n SHIFT + HOLD ALT + HOLD \n 3\n Resume the same caller\n Return to the caller from your console when ready.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Identify the need.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Place Priority Hold.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Resume the same caller.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP11","title":"Use Required Call Phrases","url":"SOP_Library/SOP11.html","text":"Use Required Call Phrases | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Use Required Call Phrases\n Use the manual\u0027s required professional phrases during common call situations.\n SOP ID SOP-11\n Manual Section CALL PHRASES\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Use the manual\u0027s required professional phrases during common call situations.\n The manual requires professional, polite, courteous language and use of “please” and “thank you,” and says not to use “uh huh,” “what,” or “umm.”\n Visual Workflow\n Open professionally\n →\n Use hold language\n →\n Return from hold\n →\n Close accurately\n Procedure\n 1\n Open professionally\n Ask who is calling using the approved opening phrase.\n 2\n Use hold language\n Ask permission before placing the caller on hold.\n 3\n Return from hold\n Thank the caller for waiting.\n 4\n Close accurately\n Repeat the callback details and confirm they are correct.\n Decision Guide\n Situation Action \n Opening May I ask who is calling, please? \n Putting on hold Can you hold, please. \n Returning from hold Thank you for waiting. May I help you? \n Patch release One moment please while I connect you to [client name]. \n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Open professionally.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Use hold language.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Return from hold.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Close accurately.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP12","title":"Verify Caller Name, Number, and Message","url":"SOP_Library/SOP12.html","text":"Verify Caller Name, Number, and Message | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Verify Caller Name, Number, and Message\n Collect and verify core caller information using the manual\u0027s approved wording.\n SOP ID SOP-12\n Manual Section CALL PHRASES\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Collect and verify core caller information using the manual\u0027s approved wording.\n Visual Workflow\n Verify spelling\n →\n Request telephone number\n →\n Repeat the number\n →\n Ask reason for call\n →\n Document refusals\n Procedure\n 1\n Verify spelling\n Ask the caller to spell their name.\n 2\n Request telephone number\n Ask for the caller\u0027s telephone number.\n 3\n Repeat the number\n Always repeat the phone number back to the caller.\n 4\n Ask reason for call\n Ask what the call is regarding / the nature of the call.\n 5\n Document refusals\n If the caller refuses information, document the situation according to account instructions.\n Suggested / Required Phrase\n Will you spell your name, please?\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Verify spelling.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Request telephone number.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Repeat the number.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Ask reason for call.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Document refusals.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP13","title":"Transfer a Call to Another Console","url":"SOP_Library/SOP13.html","text":"Transfer a Call to Another Console | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Transfer a Call to Another Console\n Transfer a caller to another Spectrum agent console.\n SOP ID SOP-13\n Manual Section TRANSFERRING A CALL\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Transfer a caller to another Spectrum agent console.\n Visual Workflow\n Initiate transfer\n →\n Enter station\n →\n Use two digits\n →\n Complete transfer\n Procedure\n 1\n Initiate transfer\n Press ALT + T or choose the Transfer shortcut.\n ALT + T \n 2\n Enter station\n Enter the destination station number.\n 3\n Use two digits\n For a one-digit station, add a leading zero (for example, 02).\n 4\n Complete transfer\n Complete the Transfer action to send the call to the selected console.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Initiate transfer.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Enter station.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Use two digits.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Complete transfer.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP14","title":"Receive a Transferred Call","url":"SOP_Library/SOP14.html","text":"Receive a Transferred Call | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Receive a Transferred Call\n Open a transferred XFER call and bring the caller live.\n SOP ID SOP-14\n Manual Section To Access a Transferred Call\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Open a transferred XFER call and bring the caller live.\n Visual Workflow\n Select XFER\n →\n Review account\n →\n Bring caller live\n Procedure\n 1\n Select XFER\n Press the corresponding TALK 1–4 key once, or click the XFER activity window.\n TALK 1–4 \n 2\n Review account\n The account screen opens; the caller is not live.\n 3\n Bring caller live\n Press ANSWER, or press the same TALK key a second time.\n ANSWER TALK 1–4 \n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Select XFER.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Review account.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Bring caller live.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP15","title":"Dismiss an Account Alert","url":"SOP_Library/SOP15.html","text":"Dismiss an Account Alert | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Dismiss an Account Alert\n Acknowledge an Account Alert so call processing can continue.\n SOP ID SOP-15\n Manual Section ACCOUNT ALERTS\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Acknowledge an Account Alert so call processing can continue.\n Visual Workflow\n Read the alert\n →\n Dismiss alert\n →\n Proceed carefully\n Procedure\n 1\n Read the alert\n Review the special condition shown in the Account Alert.\n 2\n Dismiss alert\n Press SPACEBAR to close the Alert window.\n SPACEBAR \n 3\n Proceed carefully\n Continue call processing while following the alert\u0027s instructions.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Read the alert.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Dismiss alert.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Proceed carefully.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP16","title":"Review Active Alerts During a Call","url":"SOP_Library/SOP16.html","text":"Review Active Alerts During a Call | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Review Active Alerts During a Call\n Check the Active Alerts area for important account-specific instructions while handling a caller.\n SOP ID SOP-16\n Manual Section ACTIVE ALERTS\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Check the Active Alerts area for important account-specific instructions while handling a caller.\n Visual Workflow\n Locate Active Alerts\n →\n Read current information\n →\n Act before disconnecting\n Procedure\n 1\n Locate Active Alerts\n Look in the upper-left area of the Spectrum screen.\n 2\n Read current information\n Check for instructions that may affect how the call must be handled.\n 3\n Act before disconnecting\n Follow relevant alert instructions while the caller is still on the line.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Locate Active Alerts.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Read current information.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Act before disconnecting.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP17","title":"Use the Spectrum On-Call Scheduler","url":"SOP_Library/SOP17.html","text":"Use the Spectrum On-Call Scheduler | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Use the Spectrum On-Call Scheduler\n Use the On-Call Scheduler to identify current on-call information and patching instructions.\n SOP ID SOP-17\n Manual Section Spectrum On-Call Scheduler\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Use the On-Call Scheduler to identify current on-call information and patching instructions.\n Operators are not expected to edit the On-Call Scheduler.\n Visual Workflow\n Locate the scheduler\n →\n Review schedule\n →\n Check patching directions\n →\n Use account-specific shortcut\n Procedure\n 1\n Locate the scheduler\n Find the On-Call Scheduler to the left of the message-ticket area.\n 2\n Review schedule\n Look for current on-call personnel and instructions.\n 3\n Check patching directions\n Look specifically for patching instructions when applicable.\n 4\n Use account-specific shortcut\n For configured Russ Lyon accounts, the manual notes you can patch by double-clicking the on-call agent\u0027s name.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Locate the scheduler.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Review schedule.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Check patching directions.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Use account-specific shortcut.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP18","title":"Route a Caller to an On-Duty Spanish Speaker","url":"SOP_Library/SOP18.html","text":"Route a Caller to an On-Duty Spanish Speaker | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Route a Caller to an On-Duty Spanish Speaker\n Identify and transfer a Spanish-speaking caller to an on-duty Spanish-speaking dispatcher/operator.\n SOP ID SOP-18\n Manual Section WHEN CALLERS REQUEST A SPANISH SPEAKER\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Identify and transfer a Spanish-speaking caller to an on-duty Spanish-speaking dispatcher/operator.\n Visual Workflow\n Display employee account\n →\n Select current date\n →\n Find Spanish indicator\n →\n Return to caller\n →\n Transfer\n Procedure\n 1\n Display employee account\n Press DISPLAY and enter account 0000.\n DISPLAY \n 2\n Select current date\n View the dispatcher/operators on duty.\n 3\n Find Spanish indicator\n Look for “S” next to a dispatcher/operator name.\n 4\n Return to caller\n Take the Spanish-speaking caller off hold.\n 5\n Transfer\n Transfer the caller to that dispatcher/operator\u0027s station number.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Display employee account.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Select current date.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Find Spanish indicator.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Return to caller.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Transfer.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP19","title":"Handle a Spanish Caller When No Spanish Speaker Is On Duty","url":"SOP_Library/SOP19.html","text":"Handle a Spanish Caller When No Spanish Speaker Is On Duty | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Handle a Spanish Caller When No Spanish Speaker Is On Duty\n Use the manual\u0027s backup process when no on-duty Spanish-speaking operator is available.\n SOP ID SOP-19\n Manual Section If There are No Spanish Speakers on Duty\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Use the manual\u0027s backup process when no on-duty Spanish-speaking operator is available.\n Visual Workflow\n Place Priority Hold\n →\n Display translator account\n →\n Find on-call speaker\n →\n Dial on-call speaker\n →\n Announce the account\n →\n Try backup if needed\n →\n Use translator if needed\n Procedure\n 1\n Place Priority Hold\n Place the caller on Priority Hold.\n 2\n Display translator account\n Go to account 4444 and select SPANISH SPEAKER.\n 3\n Find on-call speaker\n Locate SPANISH SPEAKER ON CALL in Special Locate.\n 4\n Dial on-call speaker\n Double-click the on-call Spanish speaker\u0027s phone number.\n 5\n Announce the account\n Announce that you have a Spanish speaker on Account XXXX.\n 6\n Try backup if needed\n If no answer, try the backup on-call.\n 7\n Use translator if needed\n If the backup does not answer, connect the caller to the Spanish translator.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Place Priority Hold.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Display translator account.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Find on-call speaker.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Dial on-call speaker.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Announce the account.\n Complete step 6 correctly: Try backup if needed.\n Complete step 7 correctly: Use translator if needed.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP20","title":"Handle Hearing or Speaking Impaired Relay Calls","url":"SOP_Library/SOP20.html","text":"Handle Hearing or Speaking Impaired Relay Calls | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Handle Hearing or Speaking Impaired Relay Calls\n Handle calls assisted by a relay-service Communications Assistant (CA).\n SOP ID SOP-20\n Manual Section HEARING/ SPEAKING IMPAIRED CALLERS\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Handle calls assisted by a relay-service Communications Assistant (CA).\n Visual Workflow\n Recognize relay assistance\n →\n Adjust pace\n →\n Address the caller directly\n →\n Signal turns\n →\n Close normally\n Procedure\n 1\n Recognize relay assistance\n The CA will identify the relay situation.\n 2\n Adjust pace\n Speak more slowly when needed.\n 3\n Address the caller directly\n Speak to the other person, not to the CA.\n 4\n Signal turns\n Say “GO AHEAD” when it is the caller\u0027s turn to speak.\n 5\n Close normally\n End with the customary thank you.\n Suggested / Required Phrase\n GO AHEAD\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Recognize relay assistance.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Adjust pace.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Address the caller directly.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Signal turns.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Close normally.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP21","title":"Open Call History","url":"SOP_Library/SOP21.html","text":"Open Call History | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Open Call History\n Display recent calls handled during the current session.\n SOP ID SOP-21\n Manual Section DISPLAYING THE LIST OF CALLS MANAGED: CALL HISTORY\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Display recent calls handled during the current session.\n Visual Workflow\n Start from Standby\n →\n Open history\n →\n Locate call\n →\n Open call\n Procedure\n 1\n Start from Standby\n Return Spectrum to Standby.\n 2\n Open history\n Press ALT + D or select History from the shortcut bar.\n ALT + D \n 3\n Locate call\n Use the arrow keys to find the desired account/time.\n 4\n Open call\n Press SELECT or click the desired entry.\n SELECT \n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Start from Standby.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Open history.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Locate call.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Open call.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP22","title":"Use the Voice Logger from Call History","url":"SOP_Library/SOP22.html","text":"Use the Voice Logger from Call History | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Use the Voice Logger from Call History\n Open a previous call recording from Call History to verify caller information.\n SOP ID SOP-22\n Manual Section SELECTING A CALL IN THE CALL HISTORY AND HOW TO LISTEN TO A CALL IN THE VOICE LOGGER\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Open a previous call recording from Call History to verify caller information.\n Visual Workflow\n Open History\n →\n Locate call\n →\n Open Voice Logger\n →\n Review recording\n Procedure\n 1\n Open History\n Select HISTORY from the Spectrum shortcut bar.\n 2\n Locate call\n Find the account/account number and call time.\n 3\n Open Voice Logger\n Right-click the call.\n 4\n Review recording\n Use the Voice Logger in the lower-right area to verify the needed information.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Open History.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Locate call.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Open Voice Logger.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Review recording.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP23","title":"Edit a Ticket Using Voice Logger","url":"SOP_Library/SOP23.html","text":"Edit a Ticket Using Voice Logger | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Edit a Ticket Using Voice Logger\n Use a call recording to verify and correct a message ticket.\n SOP ID SOP-23\n Manual Section HOW TO EDIT A TICKET USING THE VOICE LOGGER\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Use a call recording to verify and correct a message ticket.\n Visual Workflow\n Access ticket\n →\n Play recording\n →\n Correct ticket\n →\n File modification\n →\n Memo dispatcher\n Procedure\n 1\n Access ticket\n Open the ticket in IF DEL or UNDEL/REDELIV.\n 2\n Play recording\n Click the right arrow in Voice Logger.\n 3\n Correct ticket\n Edit the information if the recording shows a correction is needed.\n 4\n File modification\n Press FILE after editing.\n FILE \n 5\n Memo dispatcher\n Send a memo confirming the correction or confirming the original information was correct.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Access ticket.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Play recording.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Correct ticket.\n Complete step 4 correctly: File modification.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Memo dispatcher.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP24","title":"Review Account Information Screens","url":"SOP_Library/SOP24.html","text":"Review Account Information Screens | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Review Account Information Screens\n Review account instructions before deciding how to manage the caller.\n SOP ID SOP-24\n Manual Section ACCOUNT INFORMATION SCREENS\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Review account instructions before deciding how to manage the caller.\n Visual Workflow\n Read current account information\n →\n Determine handling\n →\n Choose correct ticket\n →\n Collect required fields\n →\n Check patch requirement\n →\n Check other instructions\n Procedure\n 1\n Read current account information\n Review the account\u0027s Information Screens.\n 2\n Determine handling\n Identify whether to take a message or refer the caller.\n 3\n Choose correct ticket\n If multiple tickets exist, identify which one applies.\n 4\n Collect required fields\n Identify all requested caller information.\n 5\n Check patch requirement\n Determine whether Patch or Announce Patch is required.\n 6\n Check other instructions\n Address any additional requirements before disconnecting.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Read current account information.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Determine handling.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Choose correct ticket.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Collect required fields.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Check patch requirement.\n Complete step 6 correctly: Check other instructions.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP25","title":"Classify an Emergency vs. Routine Matter","url":"SOP_Library/SOP25.html","text":"Classify an Emergency vs. Routine Matter | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Classify an Emergency vs. Routine Matter\n Use the account\u0027s criteria to distinguish emergency matters from routine matters.\n SOP ID SOP-25\n Manual Section ACCOUNT INFORMATION SCREENS\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Use the account\u0027s criteria to distinguish emergency matters from routine matters.\n The manual emphasizes that a situation may be an emergency for one account but routine for another.\n Visual Workflow\n Read account criteria\n →\n Assess urgency\n →\n Ask caller if uncertain\n →\n Escalate doubt\n Procedure\n 1\n Read account criteria\n Review the account instructions because emergencies differ by account.\n 2\n Assess urgency\n Determine whether the situation can wait until normal office hours.\n 3\n Ask caller if uncertain\n If uncertain, ask whether the caller feels it is an emergency.\n 4\n Escalate doubt\n If still uncertain, ask the dispatcher before deciding.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Read account criteria.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Assess urgency.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Ask caller if uncertain.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Escalate doubt.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP26","title":"Apply Relay Instructions","url":"SOP_Library/SOP26.html","text":"Apply Relay Instructions | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Apply Relay Instructions\n Use the account\u0027s relay instruction to decide whether to refer, hold, pass, or patch a call.\n SOP ID SOP-26\n Manual Section TYPES OF RELAYS\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Use the account\u0027s relay instruction to decide whether to refer, hold, pass, or patch a call.\n Visual Workflow\n Locate relay\n →\n Identify relay type\n →\n Follow that workflow\n →\n Document FOR field\n Procedure\n 1\n Locate relay\n Read the relay information in the account Information Box.\n 2\n Identify relay type\n Determine whether the account says RTN REF OFC, HLD RTN, PASS ALL/TAKE ALL, PATCH/PATCH ALL, or ANNOUNCE PATCH.\n 3\n Follow that workflow\n Handle the call according to the selected relay.\n 4\n Document FOR field\n Enter the routing/documentation required by that relay.\n Decision Guide\n Situation Action \n RTN REF OFC Take after-hours messages only when emergency criteria are met; routine callers are referred to office hours. \n HLD RTN Take routine messages and enter HLD RTN in the FOR field. \n PASS ALL / TAKE ALL Take all messages; use OFFICE for non-emergency and ON CALL for emergency as directed. \n PATCH / PATCH ALL Patch to client/extension; manual says no message ticket is required. \n ANNOUNCE PATCH Open ticket, collect requested information, then Announce Patch and document *Patched. \n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Locate relay.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Identify relay type.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Follow that workflow.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Document FOR field.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP27","title":"Display Expanded Locate Information (ELI)","url":"SOP_Library/SOP27.html","text":"Display Expanded Locate Information (ELI) | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Display Expanded Locate Information (ELI)\n Display and toggle the Expanded Locate Instructions for accounts that use them.\n SOP ID SOP-27\n Manual Section EXPANDED LOCATE INFORMATION (ELI)\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Display and toggle the Expanded Locate Instructions for accounts that use them.\n Agents view ELI but do not edit it; client-requested ELI changes are transferred to the dispatcher.\n Visual Workflow\n Display account\n →\n Open ELI\n →\n Alternative toggle\n →\n Review instructions\n →\n Toggle back\n Procedure\n 1\n Display account\n Open the relevant account.\n 2\n Open ELI\n Press DISPLAY then EDIT LOCATE.\n DISPLAY EDIT LOCATE \n 3\n Alternative toggle\n Press the * key on the numeric keypad.\n * \n 4\n Review instructions\n Read the ELI for on-call/contact instructions.\n 5\n Toggle back\n Use * to toggle back to the first Information Screen when needed.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Display account.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Open ELI.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Alternative toggle.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Review instructions.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Toggle back.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP28","title":"Check Special Locate on Every Call","url":"SOP_Library/SOP28.html","text":"Check Special Locate on Every Call | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Check Special Locate on Every Call\n Review Special Locate for temporary instructions before completing call handling.\n SOP ID SOP-28\n Manual Section THE SPECIAL LOCATE\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Review Special Locate for temporary instructions before completing call handling.\n The manual warns that not following Special Locate instructions may delay an emergency call-out.\n Visual Workflow\n Answer/display account\n →\n Read Special Locate\n →\n Identify temporary instructions\n →\n Follow before disconnecting\n Procedure\n 1\n Answer/display account\n Open the account for the current call.\n 2\n Read Special Locate\n Look at Special Locate immediately.\n 3\n Identify temporary instructions\n Check for closures, forwarding, patch sequences, emergency rules, or on-call changes.\n 4\n Follow before disconnecting\n Complete the temporary instruction while the caller is still available.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Answer/display account.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Read Special Locate.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Identify temporary instructions.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Follow before disconnecting.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP29","title":"Review All Locates at Start of Shift","url":"SOP_Library/SOP29.html","text":"Review All Locates at Start of Shift | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Review All Locates at Start of Shift\n Review current temporary account changes at the beginning of a shift.\n SOP ID SOP-29\n Manual Section THE SPECIAL LOCATE\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Review current temporary account changes at the beginning of a shift.\n Visual Workflow\n Open LOC/IF\n →\n Cycle through locates\n →\n Note temporary changes\n →\n Apply during calls\n Procedure\n 1\n Open LOC/IF\n Use the LOC/IF button on the right side of Spectrum.\n 2\n Cycle through locates\n Click through all current LOCATES.\n 3\n Note temporary changes\n Pay attention to office closures, forwarding, patch instructions, and on-call changes.\n 4\n Apply during calls\n Use those instructions when the affected accounts ring.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Open LOC/IF.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Cycle through locates.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Note temporary changes.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Apply during calls.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP30","title":"Edit Special Locate","url":"SOP_Library/SOP30.html","text":"Edit Special Locate | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Edit Special Locate\n Enter new/current short-term information into an account\u0027s Special Locate.\n SOP ID SOP-30\n Manual Section TO DELETE/LOCATE EDIT\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Enter new/current short-term information into an account\u0027s Special Locate.\n Visual Workflow\n Open account\n →\n Open Locate Edit\n →\n Enter current information\n →\n File update\n Procedure\n 1\n Open account\n Answer a call or display the account.\n 2\n Open Locate Edit\n Press DELETE/LOCATE EDIT.\n DELETE / LOCATE EDIT \n 3\n Enter current information\n Type the new/current locate information.\n 4\n File update\n Press FILE; the manual notes the border will appear purple.\n FILE \n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Open account.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Open Locate Edit.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Enter current information.\n Complete step 4 correctly: File update.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP31","title":"Document an On-Call Change in Special Locate","url":"SOP_Library/SOP31.html","text":"Document an On-Call Change in Special Locate | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Document an On-Call Change in Special Locate\n Record on-call changes in the format shown in the manual.\n SOP ID SOP-31\n Manual Section A SPECIAL LOCATE FOR ON CALL CHANGES MUST LOOK LIKE THIS\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Record on-call changes in the format shown in the manual.\n Never give out phone numbers unless the account clearly states REFER or MGO.\n Visual Workflow\n Verify contact exists\n →\n Enter on-call name\n →\n Enter effective-through date/time\n →\n Add cross-account/reference details if applicable\n →\n Escalate missing contact\n Procedure\n 1\n Verify contact exists\n Confirm the doctor/client is listed on screen with contact information.\n 2\n Enter on-call name\n Document the doctor/person on call.\n 3\n Enter effective-through date/time\n Include the TL (through) date/time.\n 4\n Add cross-account/reference details if applicable\n Use DISPLAY ACCT or REFER wording only when the manual/account calls for it.\n 5\n Escalate missing contact\n Ask the dispatcher before disconnecting if the contact is not listed.\n Decision Guide\n Situation Action \n Medical DR (name) O/C TL (date) \n Other (name) O/C TL (date) or O/C: (name) TL (date) \n Backup B/U: (name) TL (date) \n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Verify contact exists.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Enter on-call name.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Enter effective-through date/time.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Add cross-account/reference details if applicable.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Escalate missing contact.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP32","title":"Use Hypertext Commands","url":"SOP_Library/SOP32.html","text":"Use Hypertext Commands | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Use Hypertext Commands\n Activate and execute blue-dot Hypertext prompts in Spectrum.\n SOP ID SOP-32\n Manual Section USING HYPERTEXT COMMANDS\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Activate and execute blue-dot Hypertext prompts in Spectrum.\n Hypertext can display screens/accounts, speed-dial, select templates, insert keystrokes, or open scripting. Commands unavailable in the current console state cannot be highlighted.\n Visual Workflow\n Activate prompts\n →\n Move to command\n →\n Execute\n →\n Confirm result\n Procedure\n 1\n Activate prompts\n Press SHIFT + SELECT or click once on the Information Screen.\n SHIFT + SELECT \n 2\n Move to command\n Use arrow keys or point to the desired prompt.\n 3\n Execute\n Press SELECT again or click the desired command.\n SELECT \n 4\n Confirm result\n Verify that Spectrum performed the intended action.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Activate prompts.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Move to command.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Execute.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Confirm result.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP33","title":"Create a Standard Message Ticket","url":"SOP_Library/SOP33.html","text":"Create a Standard Message Ticket | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Create a Standard Message Ticket\n Open, complete, and file a standard Spectrum message ticket.\n SOP ID SOP-33\n Manual Section TYPES OF MESSAGES — Message Tickets with NO Labeling\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Open, complete, and file a standard Spectrum message ticket.\n Visual Workflow\n Open ticket\n →\n Read instructions\n →\n Enter caller information\n →\n Complete routing fields\n →\n Review\n →\n File\n Procedure\n 1\n Open ticket\n Press IF/ENTER MSG.\n IF / ENTER MSG \n 2\n Read instructions\n Use the account Information Screens; use Page Up/Page Down if needed.\n 3\n Enter caller information\n Collect information in the order requested by the account.\n 4\n Complete routing fields\n Mark ER Y/N and enter Ofc or O/C in FOR when applicable.\n 5\n Review\n Verify names, numbers, spelling, and message content.\n 6\n File\n Press FILE.\n FILE \n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Open ticket.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Read instructions.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Enter caller information.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Complete routing fields.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Review.\n Complete step 6 correctly: File.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP34","title":"Complete an Auto-Filled Message Ticket","url":"SOP_Library/SOP34.html","text":"Complete an Auto-Filled Message Ticket | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Complete an Auto-Filled Message Ticket\n Complete a message ticket that opens automatically or uses predefined reasons.\n SOP ID SOP-34\n Manual Section AUTO FILLED MESSAGE TICKETS\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Complete a message ticket that opens automatically or uses predefined reasons.\n Visual Workflow\n Open/receive ticket\n →\n Select reason\n →\n Review required information\n →\n File ticket\n Procedure\n 1\n Open/receive ticket\n Press IF/ENTER MSG, or use the ticket that automatically appears after ANSWER.\n 2\n Select reason\n Choose the appropriate reason from the available options.\n 3\n Review required information\n Confirm the ticket reflects the call accurately.\n 4\n File ticket\n Press FILE.\n FILE \n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Open/receive ticket.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Select reason.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Review required information.\n Complete step 4 correctly: File ticket.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP35","title":"Write an Effective and Accurate Message","url":"SOP_Library/SOP35.html","text":"Write an Effective and Accurate Message | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Write an Effective and Accurate Message\n Document clear, accurate messages that can be understood and acted on by the dispatcher/client.\n SOP ID SOP-35\n Manual Section WRITING EFFECTIVE/ACCURATE MESSAGE TICKETS\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Document clear, accurate messages that can be understood and acted on by the dispatcher/client.\n The manual says confirmation of numbers, addresses, and names is mandatory.\n Visual Workflow\n Confirm identifiers\n →\n Capture who/what/when/where\n →\n Use clear language\n →\n Write in first person\n →\n Review before filing\n Procedure\n 1\n Confirm identifiers\n Verify spelling of names, phone numbers, and addresses.\n 2\n Capture who/what/when/where\n Include all relevant facts.\n 3\n Use clear language\n Use accurate grammar, spelling, and appropriate descriptive words.\n 4\n Write in first person\n Write as if the caller is speaking: I, me, my, we, our.\n 5\n Review before filing\n Read the message for accuracy and completeness.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Confirm identifiers.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Capture who/what/when/where.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Use clear language.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Write in first person.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Review before filing.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP36","title":"Add Side Documentation to a Message","url":"SOP_Library/SOP36.html","text":"Add Side Documentation to a Message | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Add Side Documentation to a Message\n Add standardized side documentation when an exception or delivery result needs to be explained.\n SOP ID SOP-36\n Manual Section SIDE DOCUMENTATION\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Add standardized side documentation when an exception or delivery result needs to be explained.\n Visual Workflow\n Identify exception\n →\n Choose approved notation\n →\n Place notation correctly\n →\n Review before filing\n Procedure\n 1\n Identify exception\n Determine what happened that needs additional documentation.\n 2\n Choose approved notation\n Use the applicable side-documentation code.\n 3\n Place notation correctly\n Add the notation in the FOR field and/or message body as directed by the workflow.\n 4\n Review before filing\n Make sure the notation matches what actually happened.\n Decision Guide\n Situation Action \n *N/A No answer \n *BKL NO ANSWR Backline no answer \n *VM FULL Voicemail full \n *CLR INSISTS ER Caller insists emergency \n *2ND / 3RD CL Second or third call \n *CANCEL MESSAGE Cancellation \n *PATCHED Caller patched \n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Identify exception.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Choose approved notation.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Place notation correctly.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Review before filing.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP37","title":"Switch Between Overwrite and Insert Mode","url":"SOP_Library/SOP37.html","text":"Switch Between Overwrite and Insert Mode | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Switch Between Overwrite and Insert Mode\n Control whether new text overwrites existing text or is inserted into the message.\n SOP ID SOP-37\n Manual Section INSERTING AND OVERWRITING TEXT\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Control whether new text overwrites existing text or is inserted into the message.\n Visual Workflow\n Recognize default\n →\n Switch to insert\n →\n Enter text\n →\n Return to overwrite\n Procedure\n 1\n Recognize default\n Spectrum defaults to OVR (Overwrite) mode.\n 2\n Switch to insert\n Press INSERT when you need to insert text without replacing existing characters.\n INSERT \n 3\n Enter text\n Type the correction/addition.\n 4\n Return to overwrite\n Press INSERT again to return to OVR mode.\n INSERT \n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Recognize default.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Switch to insert.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Enter text.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Return to overwrite.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP38","title":"Resolve Incomplete Messages","url":"SOP_Library/SOP38.html","text":"Resolve Incomplete Messages | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Resolve Incomplete Messages\n Complete messages that were moved to the Incomplete stack.\n SOP ID SOP-38\n Manual Section INCOMPLETES\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Complete messages that were moved to the Incomplete stack.\n The manual says STAT, STEMI, or calls that must be passed ASAP should not be allowed to go to the Incomplete stack.\n Visual Workflow\n Stop accumulating\n →\n Open first incomplete\n →\n Complete ticket\n →\n Open next incomplete\n →\n Repeat\n Procedure\n 1\n Stop accumulating\n Do not allow more than three Incompletes; stop answering and finish them if you reach three.\n 2\n Open first incomplete\n From Standby, press ESC twice.\n ESC ESC \n 3\n Complete ticket\n Finish the work and press FILE.\n FILE \n 4\n Open next incomplete\n Press ESC twice again.\n 5\n Repeat\n Continue until all incomplete tickets are filed.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Stop accumulating.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Open first incomplete.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Complete ticket.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Open next incomplete.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Repeat.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP39","title":"Cycle Through the Incomplete Stack","url":"SOP_Library/SOP39.html","text":"Cycle Through the Incomplete Stack | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Cycle Through the Incomplete Stack\n Move through multiple incomplete messages to find the one you need.\n SOP ID SOP-39\n Manual Section TO FLIP THROUGH THE INCOMPLETE MESSAGE STACK\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Move through multiple incomplete messages to find the one you need.\n Visual Workflow\n Open first incomplete\n →\n Move current item to bottom\n →\n Open next\n →\n Repeat\n Procedure\n 1\n Open first incomplete\n Press ESC twice.\n ESC ESC \n 2\n Move current item to bottom\n Press SAVE.\n SAVE \n 3\n Open next\n Press ESC twice.\n ESC ESC \n 4\n Repeat\n Continue SAVE → ESC twice until the desired ticket appears.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Open first incomplete.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Move current item to bottom.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Open next.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Repeat.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP40","title":"Edit an Undelivered Message with SAVE","url":"SOP_Library/SOP40.html","text":"Edit an Undelivered Message with SAVE | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Edit an Undelivered Message with SAVE\n Re-open and edit an undelivered message ticket.\n SOP ID SOP-40\n Manual Section USING THE COPY/SAVE KEY TO EDIT MESSAGES\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Re-open and edit an undelivered message ticket.\n This manual section is explicitly marked as being updated. Follow current supervisor/dispatcher direction if local procedure has changed.\n Visual Workflow\n Open desired message\n →\n Re-open ticket\n →\n Make corrections\n →\n File changes\n Procedure\n 1\n Open desired message\n From Delivering Msg, press SELECT on the message.\n SELECT \n 2\n Re-open ticket\n Press SAVE; the cursor returns to the FOR field.\n SAVE \n 3\n Make corrections\n Edit the necessary information.\n 4\n File changes\n Press FILE. The manual notes the modified message is marked with S.\n FILE \n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Open desired message.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Re-open ticket.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Make corrections.\n Complete step 4 correctly: File changes.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP41","title":"Document a Second/Third Call or Cancellation","url":"SOP_Library/SOP41.html","text":"Document a Second/Third Call or Cancellation | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Document a Second/Third Call or Cancellation\n Create new documentation when a caller reports a second/third call or wants to cancel a prior message.\n SOP ID SOP-41\n Manual Section DOCUMENTATION FOR 2ND AND 3RD CALLS OR CANCELING A MESSAGE\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Create new documentation when a caller reports a second/third call or wants to cancel a prior message.\n The manual labels this section as being updated. Preserve current local supervisor/dispatcher procedure if it differs.\n Visual Workflow\n Create new ticket\n →\n Reconfirm number\n →\n Add side documentation\n →\n Copy prior information if needed\n →\n File new ticket\n Procedure\n 1\n Create new ticket\n Open a new message ticket for the new call.\n 2\n Reconfirm number\n On a second call, always reconfirm the caller\u0027s phone number.\n 3\n Add side documentation\n Document *2ND, *3RD, or CANCEL as appropriate.\n 4\n Copy prior information if needed\n Use ALT + COPY when appropriate to copy the previous ticket into a new ticket.\n ALT + COPY \n 5\n File new ticket\n Press FILE.\n FILE \n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Create new ticket.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Reconfirm number.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Add side documentation.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Copy prior information if needed.\n Complete step 5 correctly: File new ticket.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP42","title":"Deliver Undelivered Messages to a Client","url":"SOP_Library/SOP42.html","text":"Deliver Undelivered Messages to a Client | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Deliver Undelivered Messages to a Client\n Verbally relay undelivered messages to a client and move them to the Delivered stack.\n SOP ID SOP-42\n Manual Section DELIVERING MESSAGES\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Verbally relay undelivered messages to a client and move them to the Delivered stack.\n When all are delivered, the manual says the screen will show “No Undelivered” and “All Delivered.”\n Visual Workflow\n Display client account\n →\n Check Undelivered\n →\n Open Delivering Msg\n →\n Enter recipient\n →\n Record recipient\n →\n Open first message\n →\n Mark delivered\n →\n Repeat\n Procedure\n 1\n Display client account\n Open the client\u0027s account.\n 2\n Check Undelivered\n Look for pending messages and advise the client that messages are waiting.\n 3\n Open Delivering Msg\n Press IF/DELIVER MSG.\n IF / DELIVER MSG \n 4\n Enter recipient\n Type the client\u0027s name in the Deliver To Field.\n 5\n Record recipient\n Press SELECT.\n SELECT \n 6\n Open first message\n Press SELECT again and relay the message beginning with date/time.\n SELECT \n 7\n Mark delivered\n Press FILE and move to the next message.\n FILE \n 8\n Repeat\n Arrow to each remaining message and repeat until all are delivered.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Display client account.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Check Undelivered.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Open Delivering Msg.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Enter recipient.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Record recipient.\n Complete step 6 correctly: Open first message.\n Complete step 7 correctly: Mark delivered.\n Complete step 8 correctly: Repeat.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP43","title":"Handle an Office Check-Out / Phone Forwarding Call","url":"SOP_Library/SOP43.html","text":"Handle an Office Check-Out / Phone Forwarding Call | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Handle an Office Check-Out / Phone Forwarding Call\n Document when an office forwards phones, leaves for lunch/a meeting, or leaves for the day/weekend.\n SOP ID SOP-43\n Manual Section OFFICES CHECK OUT\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Document when an office forwards phones, leaves for lunch/a meeting, or leaves for the day/weekend.\n Visual Workflow\n Check Caller ID\n →\n Identify status\n →\n Get time frame\n →\n Get on-call instructions\n →\n Update Special Locate\n →\n Notify dispatcher\n Procedure\n 1\n Check Caller ID\n Look at Caller ID before placing the office caller on hold.\n 2\n Identify status\n Determine whether the office is at lunch, in a meeting, forwarding, or leaving for day/weekend.\n 3\n Get time frame\n Record when the office will return or how long the condition applies.\n 4\n Get on-call instructions\n Ask who is on call and how emergency/routine calls should be handled.\n 5\n Update Special Locate\n Document the current checkout/forwarding information.\n 6\n Notify dispatcher\n Tell the dispatcher what the client advised.\n Decision Guide\n Situation Action \n Lunch OTL \n Meeting C/F IN MTG TL [time] \n Gone for day GFD \n Gone for weekend GFWKND \n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Check Caller ID.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Identify status.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Get time frame.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Get on-call instructions.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Update Special Locate.\n Complete step 6 correctly: Notify dispatcher.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP44","title":"Collect On-Call Information from an Office","url":"SOP_Library/SOP44.html","text":"Collect On-Call Information from an Office | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Collect On-Call Information from an Office\n Collect the minimum information required when an office provides an on-call change.\n SOP ID SOP-44\n Manual Section OFFICES CHECK OUT\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Collect the minimum information required when an office provides an on-call change.\n If instructions are in-depth or confusing, alert the dispatcher and transfer the client as directed. The manual says to tell the client you will transfer them to the dispatcher who can better assist, rather than saying HOLD.\n Visual Workflow\n Get on-call name\n →\n Get start/end\n →\n Get source name\n →\n Document Special Locate\n →\n Notify dispatcher\n Procedure\n 1\n Get on-call name\n Record the person/technician/doctor who is on call.\n 2\n Get start/end\n Record the start and end date/time.\n 3\n Get source name\n Record the name of the client who provided the information.\n 4\n Document Special Locate\n Enter the current on-call instructions.\n 5\n Notify dispatcher\n Tell the dispatcher exactly what the client advised.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Get on-call name.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Get start/end.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Get source name.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Document Special Locate.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Notify dispatcher.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP45","title":"Review an IF Message During a Call","url":"SOP_Library/SOP45.html","text":"Review an IF Message During a Call | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Review an IF Message During a Call\n Check IF messages for caller-specific instructions while handling an account.\n SOP ID SOP-45\n Manual Section “IF” MESSAGES\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Check IF messages for caller-specific instructions while handling an account.\n Visual Workflow\n Look for IF messages\n →\n Read intended recipient/situation\n →\n Follow instruction\n →\n Do not ignore carry-over text\n Procedure\n 1\n Look for IF messages\n When answering, quickly check whether the account has an IF message.\n 2\n Read intended recipient/situation\n Confirm the IF message applies to the current caller or situation.\n 3\n Follow instruction\n Carry out the instruction while the caller is on the line.\n 4\n Do not ignore carry-over text\n If the IF message uses arrows across fields, read it across as instructed.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Look for IF messages.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Read intended recipient/situation.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Follow instruction.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Do not ignore carry-over text.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP46","title":"Create an IF Message","url":"SOP_Library/SOP46.html","text":"Create an IF Message | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Create an IF Message\n Create an internal IF message for a specific person or situation.\n SOP ID SOP-46\n Manual Section To Create An “IF” Message\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Create an internal IF message for a specific person or situation.\n Visual Workflow\n Display account\n →\n Open IF message entry\n →\n Complete fields\n →\n Name the target\n →\n File\n Procedure\n 1\n Display account\n Open the relevant account.\n 2\n Open IF message entry\n Press SHIFT + IF ENTER.\n SHIFT + IF ENTER \n 3\n Complete fields\n Fill in the IF Message ticket.\n 4\n Name the target\n Put the person\u0027s name or situation in the FOR field.\n 5\n File\n Press FILE.\n FILE \n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Display account.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Open IF message entry.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Complete fields.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Name the target.\n Complete step 5 correctly: File.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP47","title":"Cancel an Unwanted IF Message","url":"SOP_Library/SOP47.html","text":"Cancel an Unwanted IF Message | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Cancel an Unwanted IF Message\n Exit and cancel an unwanted IF message without filing it.\n SOP ID SOP-47\n Manual Section To escape from an unwanted IF Message\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Exit and cancel an unwanted IF message without filing it.\n Visual Workflow\n Escape message\n →\n Confirm cancellation\n Procedure\n 1\n Escape message\n Press ESC twice.\n ESC ESC \n 2\n Confirm cancellation\n When prompted, press C to cancel.\n C \n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Escape message.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Confirm cancellation.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP48","title":"Patch a Call Using Hypertext","url":"SOP_Library/SOP48.html","text":"Patch a Call Using Hypertext | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Patch a Call Using Hypertext\n Connect an inbound caller to a client using a Spectrum hypertext speed-dial.\n SOP ID SOP-48\n Manual Section THREE WAYS TO PATCH A CALL — How to PATCH\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Connect an inbound caller to a client using a Spectrum hypertext speed-dial.\n Visual Workflow\n Prepare caller\n →\n Start patch\n →\n Choose talk line\n →\n Activate speed dial\n →\n Wait for ringing\n →\n Join caller\n →\n Release yourself\n Procedure\n 1\n Prepare caller\n Tell the caller you are connecting them.\n 2\n Start patch\n Press PATCH.\n PATCH \n 3\n Choose talk line\n Press the appropriate TALK 1–4 key.\n TALK 1–4 \n 4\n Activate speed dial\n Click the hypertext link once, then a second time to dial.\n 5\n Wait for ringing\n Listen until the outbound call is ringing.\n 6\n Join caller\n Press PATCH to bring the caller onto the line.\n PATCH \n 7\n Release yourself\n Press STATUS/CLEAR to disconnect from the completed patch.\n STATUS / CLEAR \n Suggested / Required Phrase\n One moment please while I connect you to [client\u0027s name].\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Prepare caller.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Start patch.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Choose talk line.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Activate speed dial.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Wait for ringing.\n Complete step 6 correctly: Join caller.\n Complete step 7 correctly: Release yourself.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP49","title":"Patch a Call by Dialing the Number","url":"SOP_Library/SOP49.html","text":"Patch a Call by Dialing the Number | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Patch a Call by Dialing the Number\n Connect an inbound caller to a client by manually dialing the outbound number.\n SOP ID SOP-49\n Manual Section How to PATCH — If Dialing the Phone Number\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Connect an inbound caller to a client by manually dialing the outbound number.\n Visual Workflow\n Start patch\n →\n Choose talk line\n →\n Open dialing\n →\n Enter phone number\n →\n Dial\n →\n Join caller\n →\n Release yourself\n Procedure\n 1\n Start patch\n Press PATCH.\n PATCH \n 2\n Choose talk line\n Press TALK 1–4.\n TALK 1–4 \n 3\n Open dialing\n Press DIAL.\n DIAL \n 4\n Enter phone number\n Key in the destination number.\n 5\n Dial\n Press DIAL a second time.\n DIAL \n 6\n Join caller\n When ringing, press PATCH.\n PATCH \n 7\n Release yourself\n Press STATUS/CLEAR.\n STATUS / CLEAR \n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Start patch.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Choose talk line.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Open dialing.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Enter phone number.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Dial.\n Complete step 6 correctly: Join caller.\n Complete step 7 correctly: Release yourself.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP50","title":"Announce Patch a Caller","url":"SOP_Library/SOP50.html","text":"Announce Patch a Caller | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Announce Patch a Caller\n Collect the required caller information, announce the caller to the client, then connect the parties.\n SOP ID SOP-50\n Manual Section ANNOUNCE PATCH\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Collect the required caller information, announce the caller to the client, then connect the parties.\n For medical accounts, the manual says “Patch to Dr. O/C” means Announce Patch.\n Visual Workflow\n Open message ticket\n →\n Prepare caller\n →\n Start patch\n →\n Dial client\n →\n Announce caller\n →\n Get permission\n →\n Release yourself\n →\n Document result\n Procedure\n 1\n Open message ticket\n Collect the information requested by the account before patching.\n 2\n Prepare caller\n Tell the caller you are connecting them.\n 3\n Start patch\n Press PATCH, then TALK 1–4.\n PATCH TALK 1–4 \n 4\n Dial client\n Use hypertext or dial the client\u0027s number.\n 5\n Announce caller\n When the client answers, identify yourself and the caller; provide the reason if appropriate.\n 6\n Get permission\n If the client agrees, press PATCH to bring the caller online.\n PATCH \n 7\n Release yourself\n Press STATUS/CLEAR.\n STATUS / CLEAR \n 8\n Document result\n Review the ticket and document *Patched in the FOR field and call notes.\n Suggested / Required Phrase\n Hello, this is [your name] with the answering service. I have [caller\u0027s name] calling for you.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Open message ticket.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Prepare caller.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Start patch.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Dial client.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Announce caller.\n Complete step 6 correctly: Get permission.\n Complete step 7 correctly: Release yourself.\n Complete step 8 correctly: Document result.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP51","title":"Handle No Answer During an Announce Patch","url":"SOP_Library/SOP51.html","text":"Handle No Answer During an Announce Patch | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Handle No Answer During an Announce Patch\n Protect the caller from being sent into client voicemail and convert the call to a message when the client does not answer.\n SOP ID SOP-51\n Manual Section ANNOUNCE PATCH — No Answer / Voicemail\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Protect the caller from being sent into client voicemail and convert the call to a message when the client does not answer.\n Visual Workflow\n Recognize voicemail\n →\n Disconnect outbound call\n →\n Advise caller\n →\n Take message\n →\n Disconnect caller\n →\n Document\n →\n File\n Procedure\n 1\n Recognize voicemail\n As soon as voicemail answers, do not release the caller into it.\n 2\n Disconnect outbound call\n Press STATUS/CLEAR; this disconnects the outbound call and brings the caller back.\n STATUS / CLEAR \n 3\n Advise caller\n Tell the caller the client is unavailable and offer to take a message.\n 4\n Take message\n Collect the required message and thank the caller.\n 5\n Disconnect caller\n Press STATUS/CLEAR.\n STATUS / CLEAR \n 6\n Document\n Enter *N/A in the FOR field/call notes and review the message.\n 7\n File\n Press FILE.\n FILE \n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Recognize voicemail.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Disconnect outbound call.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Advise caller.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Take message.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Disconnect caller.\n Complete step 6 correctly: Document.\n Complete step 7 correctly: File.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP52","title":"Leave Word to Call Answering Service (LWTCAS)","url":"SOP_Library/SOP52.html","text":"Leave Word to Call Answering Service (LWTCAS) | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Leave Word to Call Answering Service (LWTCAS)\n Leave the specified voicemail instruction for a client, return to the caller, and document LWTCAS.\n SOP ID SOP-52\n Manual Section LWTCAS (Leave Word to Call Answering Service)\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Leave the specified voicemail instruction for a client, return to the caller, and document LWTCAS.\n Visual Workflow\n Reach voicemail\n →\n Leave word\n →\n Return to caller\n →\n Take caller message\n →\n Disconnect caller\n →\n Document LWTCAS\n →\n File\n Procedure\n 1\n Reach voicemail\n Follow the account\u0027s Announce Patch attempt until voicemail answers.\n 2\n Leave word\n Leave the answering-service callback message; include callback number only if the account says to.\n 3\n Return to caller\n Press STATUS/CLEAR to disconnect outbound and bring the caller back.\n STATUS / CLEAR \n 4\n Take caller message\n Advise client is unavailable and take the caller\u0027s message.\n 5\n Disconnect caller\n Press STATUS/CLEAR.\n STATUS / CLEAR \n 6\n Document LWTCAS\n Enter *LWTCAS in the FOR field and at the end of the message.\n 7\n File\n Press FILE.\n FILE \n Suggested / Required Phrase\n Please call the answering service; you have a message. Thank you.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Reach voicemail.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Leave word.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Return to caller.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Take caller message.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Disconnect caller.\n Complete step 6 correctly: Document LWTCAS.\n Complete step 7 correctly: File.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP53","title":"Leave a Tone Voice Page Message (TVP MSG)","url":"SOP_Library/SOP53.html","text":"Leave a Tone Voice Page Message (TVP MSG) | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Leave a Tone Voice Page Message (TVP MSG)\n Leave the caller\u0027s full information in client voicemail when the account specifically instructs TVP MSG.\n SOP ID SOP-53\n Manual Section TVP MSG (Tone Voice Page Message)\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Leave the caller\u0027s full information in client voicemail when the account specifically instructs TVP MSG.\n Visual Workflow\n Prepare message first\n →\n Leave full voicemail\n →\n Return to caller\n →\n Advise caller\n →\n Disconnect caller\n →\n Document\n →\n File\n Procedure\n 1\n Prepare message first\n Open a message ticket and collect all information required by the account before dialing.\n 2\n Leave full voicemail\n If the patch reaches voicemail, leave the caller\u0027s full information.\n 3\n Return to caller\n Press STATUS/CLEAR.\n STATUS / CLEAR \n 4\n Advise caller\n Tell the caller the person is unavailable and that you will let the client know they called.\n 5\n Disconnect caller\n Press STATUS/CLEAR.\n STATUS / CLEAR \n 6\n Document\n Enter *TVP MSG in the FOR field and at the end of the message.\n 7\n File\n Press FILE.\n FILE \n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Prepare message first.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Leave full voicemail.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Return to caller.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Advise caller.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Disconnect caller.\n Complete step 6 correctly: Document.\n Complete step 7 correctly: File.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP54","title":"Perform a Dual Patch","url":"SOP_Library/SOP54.html","text":"Perform a Dual Patch | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Perform a Dual Patch\n Reconnect a caller and the on-call person when the original Patch/Announce Patch was not completed.\n SOP ID SOP-54\n Manual Section DUAL PATCHING\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Reconnect a caller and the on-call person when the original Patch/Announce Patch was not completed.\n Visual Workflow\n Call caller back\n →\n Confirm caller\n →\n Priority Hold caller\n →\n Call on-call\n →\n Announce caller\n →\n Connect both parties\n →\n Document\n →\n If no answer\n Procedure\n 1\n Call caller back\n Press DIAL, select a TALK line, enter the caller\u0027s number, and press DIAL.\n DIAL TALK \n 2\n Confirm caller\n Confirm the caller\u0027s identity and tell them you will connect them to the on-call person.\n 3\n Priority Hold caller\n Place the caller on Priority Hold.\n 4\n Call on-call\n Press DIAL, select a TALK line, and select the on-call contact number.\n DIAL TALK \n 5\n Announce caller\n Tell the on-call person who is on the line and ask permission to connect.\n 6\n Connect both parties\n Press PATCH twice, then STATUS/CLEAR.\n PATCH PATCH STATUS / CLEAR \n 7\n Document\n Enter *PATCHED in the FOR field and side documentation.\n 8\n If no answer\n Document *No Answer, or LWTCAS if voicemail was left as instructed.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Call caller back.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Confirm caller.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Priority Hold caller.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Call on-call.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Announce caller.\n Complete step 6 correctly: Connect both parties.\n Complete step 7 correctly: Document.\n Complete step 8 correctly: If no answer.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP55","title":"Handle a Medical Emergency Call","url":"SOP_Library/SOP55.html","text":"Handle a Medical Emergency Call | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Handle a Medical Emergency Call\n Route medical emergency calls to the on-call doctor or nurse according to the account.\n SOP ID SOP-55\n Manual Section MEDICAL ACCOUNT INFORMATION — EMERGENCIES\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Route medical emergency calls to the on-call doctor or nurse according to the account.\n The manual says operators are not medically trained; use the account instructions and dispatcher when uncertain.\n Visual Workflow\n Read medical account instructions\n →\n Ask emergency question\n →\n Clarify uncertainty\n →\n Mark emergency correctly\n →\n Pass to on-call\n Procedure\n 1\n Read medical account instructions\n Check the account\u0027s emergency criteria and any Special Locate/On-Call information.\n 2\n Ask emergency question\n Ask whether the call is an emergency when the account requires it.\n 3\n Clarify uncertainty\n If the caller is unsure, ask whether they need the on-call physician now or can wait for the office to open.\n 4\n Mark emergency correctly\n If the caller needs a callback now, mark the message so it will be passed.\n 5\n Pass to on-call\n Follow the account\u0027s process to reach the on-call doctor/nurse.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Read medical account instructions.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Ask emergency question.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Clarify uncertainty.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Mark emergency correctly.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Pass to on-call.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP56","title":"Refer Routine Medical Calls to the Office","url":"SOP_Library/SOP56.html","text":"Refer Routine Medical Calls to the Office | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Refer Routine Medical Calls to the Office\n Identify routine medical calls that should be referred to normal office hours when the account says to do so.\n SOP ID SOP-56\n Manual Section REFER ROUTINE MESSAGES TO MEDICAL OFFICE\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Identify routine medical calls that should be referred to normal office hours when the account says to do so.\n Visual Workflow\n Read account instructions\n →\n Identify routine reason\n →\n Advise caller\n →\n Take only allowed exceptions\n Procedure\n 1\n Read account instructions\n Confirm the account refers routine calls to the office.\n 2\n Identify routine reason\n Examples in the manual include lab results, appointments, routine refills, referrals, directions, and billing.\n 3\n Advise caller\n Explain that routine matters should be handled by the office during normal business hours.\n 4\n Take only allowed exceptions\n If the account or emergency criteria provide an exception, follow that account-specific instruction.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Read account instructions.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Identify routine reason.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Advise caller.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Take only allowed exceptions.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP57","title":"Handle Same-Day Appointment or Early-Morning Surgery Cancellations","url":"SOP_Library/SOP57.html","text":"Handle Same-Day Appointment or Early-Morning Surgery Cancellations | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Handle Same-Day Appointment or Early-Morning Surgery Cancellations\n Document eligible same-day appointment or early-morning surgery cancellations for medical accounts.\n SOP ID SOP-57\n Manual Section SAME DAY APPOINTMENT CANCELLATIONS OR EARLY MORNING SURGERY CANCELLATIONS\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Document eligible same-day appointment or early-morning surgery cancellations for medical accounts.\n Visual Workflow\n Check account-specific cancellation rules\n →\n Determine timing\n →\n Collect patient data\n →\n Document cancellation\n →\n Route per account\n Procedure\n 1\n Check account-specific cancellation rules\n Some accounts differ; verify instructions.\n 2\n Determine timing\n The manual\u0027s general guideline accepts same-day cancellations up to two hours after office opening.\n 3\n Collect patient data\n Get name, phone number, date of birth, patient\u0027s doctor, appointment/surgery time/date, and cancellation reason.\n 4\n Document cancellation\n Create the message ticket with the required cancellation details.\n 5\n Route per account\n Pass/hold the cancellation as instructed by the medical account.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Check account-specific cancellation rules.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Determine timing.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Collect patient data.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Document cancellation.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Route per account.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP58","title":"Handle After-Hours Prescription Calls","url":"SOP_Library/SOP58.html","text":"Handle After-Hours Prescription Calls | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Handle After-Hours Prescription Calls\n Apply account-specific rules to after-hours prescription requests.\n SOP ID SOP-58\n Manual Section PRESCRIPTIONS\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Apply account-specific rules to after-hours prescription requests.\n The manual explicitly notes that medical accounts differ and some do not accept after-hours prescription requests at all.\n Visual Workflow\n Read prescription rules\n →\n Identify request type\n →\n Follow account exception\n →\n Document allowed reason\n →\n Escalate uncertainty\n Procedure\n 1\n Read prescription rules\n Check whether the account accepts after-hours prescriptions and under what circumstances.\n 2\n Identify request type\n Determine whether it is a routine refill, urgent pharmacy request, missed prescription, post-surgery request, or medication reaction.\n 3\n Follow account exception\n Use the account\u0027s stated exceptions rather than applying a universal rule.\n 4\n Document allowed reason\n When taking the message, document the reason/symptom as instructed.\n 5\n Escalate uncertainty\n Ask the dispatcher if the account instructions do not clearly resolve the situation.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Read prescription rules.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Identify request type.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Follow account exception.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Document allowed reason.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Escalate uncertainty.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP59","title":"Handle Medication Names, Lab Values, and Test Results","url":"SOP_Library/SOP59.html","text":"Handle Medication Names, Lab Values, and Test Results | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Handle Medication Names, Lab Values, and Test Results\n Handle sensitive medical information according to the manual\u0027s limits.\n SOP ID SOP-59\n Manual Section MEDICAL NAMES, LAB VALUES, TEST RESULTS\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Handle sensitive medical information according to the manual\u0027s limits.\n Visual Workflow\n Check account exception\n →\n Avoid restricted detail by default\n →\n Use allowed summary\n →\n Advise callback\n Procedure\n 1\n Check account exception\n Confirm whether the account specifically allows medication names, lab values, or test results.\n 2\n Avoid restricted detail by default\n The manual says not to take medication names, lab values, or test results unless the account says otherwise.\n 3\n Use allowed summary\n For medication, ask what the medication is used for; otherwise document the category such as LAB VALUES, TEST RESULTS, or MEDICATION.\n 4\n Advise callback\n Tell the caller the doctor/medical staff will return the call as appropriate.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Check account exception.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Avoid restricted detail by default.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Use allowed summary.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Advise callback.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP60","title":"Instruct a Medical Caller to Unblock Their Phone","url":"SOP_Library/SOP60.html","text":"Instruct a Medical Caller to Unblock Their Phone | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Instruct a Medical Caller to Unblock Their Phone\n Make sure a medical caller can receive the on-call doctor\u0027s or nurse\u0027s callback.\n SOP ID SOP-60\n Manual Section MEDICAL ACCOUNTS — UNBLOCK TELEPHONE LINES\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Make sure a medical caller can receive the on-call doctor\u0027s or nurse\u0027s callback.\n The manual lists *87 or *86 for unblocking; follow the current account instruction if it specifies one.\n Visual Workflow\n Check callback requirement\n →\n Give unblock instruction\n →\n Document if needed\n Procedure\n 1\n Check callback requirement\n When a medical caller is expecting a callback, confirm whether blocked calls are accepted.\n 2\n Give unblock instruction\n Instruct the caller to use the code specified in the manual/account to unblock the line.\n 3\n Document if needed\n Record the instruction or issue when account workflow requires it.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Check callback requirement.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Give unblock instruction.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Document if needed.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP61","title":"Take a Hospital Page Call","url":"SOP_Library/SOP61.html","text":"Take a Hospital Page Call | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Take a Hospital Page Call\n Collect the required information for a hospital page to the on-call doctor, NP, or PA.\n SOP ID SOP-61\n Manual Section HOSPITAL PAGE\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Collect the required information for a hospital page to the on-call doctor, NP, or PA.\n The manual warns that incorrect patient information can delay urgent medical attention.\n Visual Workflow\n Confirm call type\n →\n Check Announce Patch requirement\n →\n Collect caller/hospital contact\n →\n Collect patient identifiers\n →\n Confirm patient status\n →\n Capture nature of call\n →\n Review all data\n Procedure\n 1\n Confirm call type\n Verify the caller wants a PAGE, not a CONSULT.\n 2\n Check Announce Patch requirement\n Determine whether the account is an Announce Patch account.\n 3\n Collect caller/hospital contact\n Get caller name, hospital, phone number, and extensions; always verify the number.\n 4\n Collect patient identifiers\n Get patient name/spelling, DOB, room/bed, MRN if requested, and patient\u0027s doctor.\n 5\n Confirm patient status\n Determine new vs. established when required.\n 6\n Capture nature of call\n Ask the reason/nature of the call using appropriate terminology.\n 7\n Review all data\n Verify spelling and numbers before filing/routing.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Confirm call type.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Check Announce Patch requirement.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Collect caller/hospital contact.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Collect patient identifiers.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Confirm patient status.\n Complete step 6 correctly: Capture nature of call.\n Complete step 7 correctly: Review all data.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP62","title":"Take a Hospital Consult Call","url":"SOP_Library/SOP62.html","text":"Take a Hospital Consult Call | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Take a Hospital Consult Call\n Collect and route a hospital consultation request.\n SOP ID SOP-62\n Manual Section HOSPITAL CONSULTS\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Collect and route a hospital consultation request.\n Visual Workflow\n Confirm consult workflow\n →\n Collect patient data\n →\n Identify doctors\n →\n Determine urgency\n →\n Capture diagnosis/reason\n →\n Collect insurance if requested\n →\n Route correctly\n Procedure\n 1\n Confirm consult workflow\n Check whether the account is Announce Patch.\n 2\n Collect patient data\n Get age/DOB, room/bed, new vs. established status, and MRN as requested.\n 3\n Identify doctors\n Record which doctor the consult is for and the doctor requesting it.\n 4\n Determine urgency\n Ask whether the consult is ROUTINE, URGENT, or STAT.\n 5\n Capture diagnosis/reason\n Document the diagnosis or reason for consultation.\n 6\n Collect insurance if requested\n Enter insurance when the account/ticket requests it.\n 7\n Route correctly\n Use the required FOR-field consult designation and pass according to urgency/account instructions.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Confirm consult workflow.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Collect patient data.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Identify doctors.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Determine urgency.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Capture diagnosis/reason.\n Complete step 6 correctly: Collect insurance if requested.\n Complete step 7 correctly: Route correctly.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP63","title":"Handle Valley Pediatrics Triage Messages","url":"SOP_Library/SOP63.html","text":"Handle Valley Pediatrics Triage Messages | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Handle Valley Pediatrics Triage Messages\n Enter pediatric triage messages in the correct sub-account and system during after-hours coverage.\n SOP ID SOP-63\n Manual Section PEDIATRIC ACCOUNTS — Valley Pediatrics Triage (VPT)\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Enter pediatric triage messages in the correct sub-account and system during after-hours coverage.\n Visual Workflow\n Check availability\n →\n Use correct sub-account\n →\n Enter after-hours message\n →\n Handle second call\n →\n Transfer checking-in nurse\n Procedure\n 1\n Check availability\n Read Special Instructions/Locate for triage-nurse availability.\n 2\n Use correct sub-account\n Use the Triage Nurse sub-account .02; do not put the triage ticket on the home page.\n 3\n Enter after-hours message\n Follow the VPT website and Spectrum ticket process for the caller.\n 4\n Handle second call\n If no callback within an hour, re-enter the information on VPT and create a new Spectrum ticket with the new encounter number.\n 5\n Transfer checking-in nurse\n If the triage nurse calls to check in, transfer immediately to the dispatcher.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Check availability.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Use correct sub-account.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Enter after-hours message.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Handle second call.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Transfer checking-in nurse.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP64","title":"Take a Newborn Notification","url":"SOP_Library/SOP64.html","text":"Take a Newborn Notification | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Take a Newborn Notification\n Collect and route newborn notifications from hospitals.\n SOP ID SOP-64\n Manual Section PEDIATRIC ACCOUNTS — NEWBORN NOTIFICATIONS\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Collect and route newborn notifications from hospitals.\n Visual Workflow\n Open newborn page\n →\n Determine callback need\n →\n Collect hospital/caller data\n →\n Collect newborn details\n →\n Review and file\n Procedure\n 1\n Open newborn page\n Use the pediatric account\u0027s newborn-reporting page.\n 2\n Determine callback need\n If nurse says well baby/no callback, use NEWBORN in FOR; if callback needed, use O/C.\n 3\n Collect hospital/caller data\n Get caller/hospital and verified phone number.\n 4\n Collect newborn details\n Get sex (BG/BB), time born, weight, Apgar, delivery provider/method, well/sick status, assigned doctor, and room if requested.\n 5\n Review and file\n Verify details and route the message according to the account.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Open newborn page.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Determine callback need.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Collect hospital/caller data.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Collect newborn details.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Review and file.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP65","title":"Search the Doctor\u0027s Directory (Account 0003)","url":"SOP_Library/SOP65.html","text":"Search the Doctor\u0027s Directory (Account 0003) | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Search the Doctor\u0027s Directory (Account 0003)\n Use Account 0003 to locate a doctor\u0027s medical account information.\n SOP ID SOP-65\n Manual Section DOCTOR’S DIRECTORY ACCOUNT 0003\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Use Account 0003 to locate a doctor\u0027s medical account information.\n The manual notes you cannot enter the Doctor\u0027s Directory if an active ticket is on the screen.\n Visual Workflow\n Display Account 0003\n →\n Prepare table search\n →\n Search doctor\n →\n Verify correct doctor\n Procedure\n 1\n Display Account 0003\n Open the Doctor\u0027s Directory account.\n 2\n Prepare table search\n Remove the black checkmark before searching the doctor\u0027s name, as instructed in the manual.\n 3\n Search doctor\n Locate the doctor\u0027s first/last name and associated account information.\n 4\n Verify correct doctor\n Use available identifying information to avoid selecting the wrong physician.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Display Account 0003.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Prepare table search.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Search doctor.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Verify correct doctor.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP66","title":"Send an In-House Memo","url":"SOP_Library/SOP66.html","text":"Send an In-House Memo | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Send an In-House Memo\n Send a Spectrum memo to another signed-on employee.\n SOP ID SOP-66\n Manual Section IN HOUSE MEMO’S — Entering/Delivering\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Send a Spectrum memo to another signed-on employee.\n Visual Workflow\n Clear Spectrum screen\n →\n Open message entry\n →\n Enter recipient\n →\n Write memo\n →\n File memo\n Procedure\n 1\n Clear Spectrum screen\n Make sure the Spectrum screen is cleared.\n 2\n Open message entry\n Select IF ENTER MSG.\n IF ENTER MSG \n 3\n Enter recipient\n Enter the recipient\u0027s name and station number; add a leading zero to one-digit stations.\n 4\n Write memo\n Enter the message in the bottom box.\n 5\n File memo\n File the memo. If more space is needed, file the first memo and create another to continue.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Clear Spectrum screen.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Open message entry.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Enter recipient.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Write memo.\n Complete step 5 correctly: File memo.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP67","title":"Act on an In-House Memo","url":"SOP_Library/SOP67.html","text":"Act on an In-House Memo | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Act on an In-House Memo\n Open and respond to internal memos promptly.\n SOP ID SOP-67\n Manual Section IN HOUSE MEMO’S — Acting on a Memo\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Open and respond to internal memos promptly.\n Visual Workflow\n Open promptly\n →\n Read requested action\n →\n Complete action\n →\n Acknowledge sender\n Procedure\n 1\n Open promptly\n Open memos as soon as possible.\n 2\n Read requested action\n Determine whether the memo is informational or asks for a correction/action.\n 3\n Complete action\n Make the requested correction or response.\n 4\n Acknowledge sender\n Alert the sender/deliverer that the memo was received or the requested correction was made.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Open promptly.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Read requested action.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Complete action.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Acknowledge sender.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP68","title":"Transfer an In-House Memo","url":"SOP_Library/SOP68.html","text":"Transfer an In-House Memo | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Transfer an In-House Memo\n Transfer a memo that was sent to the wrong station or needs to be passed to another operator/dispatcher.\n SOP ID SOP-68\n Manual Section IN HOUSE MEMO’S — Transferring a Memo\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Transfer a memo that was sent to the wrong station or needs to be passed to another operator/dispatcher.\n Visual Workflow\n Identify intended recipient\n →\n Choose Transfer\n →\n Select station\n →\n Complete transfer\n Procedure\n 1\n Identify intended recipient\n Confirm where the memo should go.\n 2\n Choose Transfer\n Select TRANSFER on the shortcut bar.\n 3\n Select station\n Choose the intended operator/dispatcher station number.\n 4\n Complete transfer\n Transfer the memo to the selected station.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Identify intended recipient.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Choose Transfer.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Select station.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Complete transfer.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP69","title":"Take a Basic Message","url":"SOP_Library/SOP69.html","text":"Take a Basic Message | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Take a Basic Message\n Capture the minimum complete information expected in a basic message.\n SOP ID SOP-69\n Manual Section MISCELLANEOUS INSTRUCTIONS — A “basic” message includes\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Capture the minimum complete information expected in a basic message.\n Visual Workflow\n Get full name\n →\n Get telephone number\n →\n Get nature of call\n →\n Apply emergency criteria\n →\n Check extra account requirements\n Procedure\n 1\n Get full name\n Obtain first and last name and confirm spelling.\n 2\n Get telephone number\n Obtain area code and phone number; verify every number.\n 3\n Get nature of call\n Document why the person is calling, not just “please call.”\n 4\n Apply emergency criteria\n If the account asks whether the call is an emergency, use the account\u0027s criteria.\n 5\n Check extra account requirements\n Collect any account-specific fields highlighted/instructed on the account.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Get full name.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Get telephone number.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Get nature of call.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Apply emergency criteria.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Check extra account requirements.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP70","title":"Alert the Dispatcher for Priority Situations","url":"SOP_Library/SOP70.html","text":"Alert the Dispatcher for Priority Situations | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Alert the Dispatcher for Priority Situations\n Immediately alert the dispatcher for priority situations specifically identified by the manual.\n SOP ID SOP-70\n Manual Section MISCELLANEOUS INSTRUCTIONS\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Immediately alert the dispatcher for priority situations specifically identified by the manual.\n Visual Workflow\n Recognize priority situation\n →\n Announce aloud\n →\n Complete required ticket/call handling\n Procedure\n 1\n Recognize priority situation\n Examples listed include STAT calls, patient chest pains, Tempe School District Crisis Line account 2765, or someone stuck in an elevator.\n 2\n Announce aloud\n Alert the dispatcher immediately and make sure the dispatcher acknowledges you.\n 3\n Complete required ticket/call handling\n Finish the urgent documentation and follow account-specific routing without unnecessary delay.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Recognize priority situation.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Announce aloud.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Complete required ticket/call handling.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP71","title":"Review Operator-Memo Accounts Before Taking Calls","url":"SOP_Library/SOP71.html","text":"Review Operator-Memo Accounts Before Taking Calls | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Review Operator-Memo Accounts Before Taking Calls\n Review account changes and operator memos before or during the shift.\n SOP ID SOP-71\n Manual Section MISCELLANEOUS INSTRUCTIONS / HOW TO USE ACCOUNTS\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Review account changes and operator memos before or during the shift.\n Visual Workflow\n Check Account 3400\n →\n Initial/date when required\n →\n Check office account\n →\n Apply changes\n Procedure\n 1\n Check Account 3400\n Review account changes, complaints, and operator memos.\n 2\n Initial/date when required\n The manual says staff must initial and date that account changes/complaints were read.\n 3\n Check office account\n Review Account 4444 for applicable operator information/memos.\n 4\n Apply changes\n Use the current updates when answering affected accounts.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Check Account 3400.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Initial/date when required.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Check office account.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Apply changes.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP72","title":"Work During Spectrum Offline / Retry","url":"SOP_Library/SOP72.html","text":"Work During Spectrum Offline / Retry | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Work During Spectrum Offline / Retry\n Continue taking calls manually when Spectrum screens are offline or in retry.\n SOP ID SOP-72\n Manual Section SPECTRUM SYSTEM TROUBLE SHOOT\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Continue taking calls manually when Spectrum screens are offline or in retry.\n This troubleshooting section is labeled as a draft in the manual; current IT/supervisor procedures should take precedence if updated.\n Visual Workflow\n Recognize outage\n →\n Use outage greeting\n →\n Record account number\n →\n Write messages on paper\n →\n Alert dispatcher for emergencies\n →\n Back-enter messages\n Procedure\n 1\n Recognize outage\n If screens are not functioning but calls can still be answered, switch to manual message capture.\n 2\n Use outage greeting\n Answer with the generic manual greeting because Information Screens are unavailable.\n 3\n Record account number\n Write down the account number shown in the TALK window.\n 4\n Write messages on paper\n Capture all caller information by hand.\n 5\n Alert dispatcher for emergencies\n Immediately alert the dispatcher for an emergency call.\n 6\n Back-enter messages\n When Spectrum returns online, enter the handwritten messages into the appropriate accounts.\n Suggested / Required Phrase\n Good morning/evening, this is ___, may I help you?\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Recognize outage.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Use outage greeting.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Record account number.\n Complete step 4 correctly: Write messages on paper.\n Complete step 5 correctly: Alert dispatcher for emergencies.\n Complete step 6 correctly: Back-enter messages.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."},{"id":"SOP73","title":"Sign Off the VPN After a Remote Shift","url":"SOP_Library/SOP73.html","text":"Sign Off the VPN After a Remote Shift | Spectrum SOP \n Spectrum Operator Standard Operating Procedure\n Sign Off the VPN After a Remote Shift\n Log off the VPN at the end of a remote shift so the next operator can connect.\n SOP ID SOP-73\n Manual Section VPN — VIRTUAL PRIVATE NETWORK\n Source Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023\n Purpose\n Log off the VPN at the end of a remote shift so the next operator can connect.\n The manual emphasizes that leaving the VPN connected can prevent another operator from signing on.\n Visual Workflow\n Finish shift work\n →\n Log off VPN\n →\n Confirm disconnected\n Procedure\n 1\n Finish shift work\n Complete Spectrum sign-off and any required end-of-shift tasks.\n 2\n Log off VPN\n Disconnect/sign off the company VPN.\n 3\n Confirm disconnected\n Verify the VPN session is no longer active.\n Operator Check\n Complete step 1 correctly: Finish shift work.\n Complete step 2 correctly: Log off VPN.\n Complete step 3 correctly: Confirm disconnected.\n This job aid is derived from the uploaded Revised Spectrum Manual — July 2023. Follow account-specific Information Screens, Special Locate, Active Alerts, On-Call Scheduler instructions, and dispatcher/supervisor direction where the manual identifies account-specific exceptions or draft/updated sections."}];

